    <node id="Recurrent Neural Networks">
      <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Networks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of deep learning model architectures, including standard RNNs, LSTMs, and GRUs, tested for sentence representation.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, utilized via bidirectional variants to process recipe ingredient lists.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data, foundational to sequence-to-sequence modeling, RNNs, GRUs, and LSTMs.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep learning neural networks capable of modeling sequence data and forming short-term memory.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures (RNNs) used in sequence-to-sequence translation models and hierarchical document-level translation architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures commonly benchmarked and used for modeling sequential data and probabilistic human language.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures designed to process sequential data and recognize patterns across time, commonly used for text classification and dialogue modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures tailored for processing sequential data, used in translation and knowledge graph enrichment.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures typically employed in standard dialogue state tracking models.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of sequential neural network architectures, including LSTMs, used in dialogue systems to capture temporal dependencies, often introducing latency bottlenecks.&lt;SEP&gt;A family of neural architectures including RNNs, GRUs, and LSTMs that capture long-range dependencies in sequential text data.&lt;SEP&gt;A family of neural network architectures designed for sequential data, utilized by models such as GLAD, GCE, and StateNet_PSI.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) are a family of neural network architectures suited for sequential processing, applied in standard sequence-to-sequence translation models.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurrent neural networks (RNNs) are a category of deep learning models designed for processing sequential data and variable-length text representations.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurrent neural networks are deep learning model architectures used as state-of-the-art systems for keyphrase generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sequential deep learning architectures (RNNs) utilized for natural language processing and sentiment analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9fdc4a98dc4d2c8f6875739e4d466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c233285dd27a358f6bf38c2050006d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3bf41e0b7ea425266139faf090ad226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a0c631645254ecce4e14a53d44a991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb3ab7fc50f538bef2c8ddb57a8a6b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e9f52662c01528fd8d607b1462c48df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f148e57eed21f7948ba04d2d12e56d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298f7bb76f5ebb6d2dd7ddc9afddde09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58403a931bb26f8c20e17e82757f13f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bc49e88e2b4d9c426436c1d272e949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a91d0fd0db145647734eeea856cd2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6147035553ac26ef0837a5ab654f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45dd962c5b788395b9105c9472288d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f5016d3aa81277cabc5c947f1ca64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Long Short-Term Memory">
      <data key="d0">Long Short-Term Memory</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of recurrent neural network architectures designed to process sequential data while capturing word order and long-term dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;A gated recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture designed to solve the vanishing and exploding gradient problems in sequence modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture (LSTM RNN) employed within the encoders and decoders of the generative models.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture designed to capture long-range sequence dependencies, commonly employed in encoder-decoder systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture designed to process sequential data, frequently employed as a decoder in sequence generation tasks like image captioning.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture variant used within the encoder component of dialogue state tracking implementations.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network variant used to process sequential data and construct embeddings from character representations.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized category of recurrent neural network architecture chosen as the primary model due to outperforming other variants.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized category of recurrent neural network architecture units designed to capture sequential dependencies, utilized for encoding ingredient representations.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized recurrent neural network architecture designed to model temporal sequences and long-range dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized recurrent neural network unit architecture designed to capture long-range dependencies and optimize gradient propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific recurrent neural network architecture designed to model temporal sequences and long-range dependencies, used as a language model.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of recurrent neural network architecture utilized in tri-LSTM and sequence-to-sequence encoders and decoders for processing conversation tokens and assertions.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture concatenated with language vectors in the presented multilingual model.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture designed to capture long-range dependencies in sequence data, utilized in the toolkit's hidden units.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture designed to model long-range temporal dependencies in sequential data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture used as non-linear activation functions in both the encoder and decoder components of the text simplification models.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network unit designed to capture dependencies in sequential text data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b32cb050de56f58b5792720c6bc3e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b98e14081bd42f130f547ac6df8114f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdef2f67b0ab332d8da79c41fb0e58c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab274e4799f62f2fbfabf369fb71267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a0c631645254ecce4e14a53d44a991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90c3963b2880a766180f3aafb75b379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8ad7bf1880d82f40811c2078046e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76f1c0c2ed37a786263a6a6d8b0bb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2af0dac5bc5afdea73673fd2462c1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298f7bb76f5ebb6d2dd7ddc9afddde09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626602288681ee562ad75771b687c6be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4f52a592e1970d14c92e285c600305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ae86766195404daaa0c376964357ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bc49e88e2b4d9c426436c1d272e949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a91d0fd0db145647734eeea856cd2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6147035553ac26ef0837a5ab654f4f</data>
    </node>
