    <node id="Semantic Web">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Web</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A web data initiative and technological framework facilitating machine-readable structured information, renewing interest in ontology-based natural language generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Web encompasses standards, technologies, and ontologies providing structured semantic knowledge and data representation to aid disambiguation and reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Web is a technology domain and framework offering structured semantic representations and technologies to address lexical and syntactic ambiguity in text processing and translation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Semantic Web is an extension of the World Wide Web aimed at making data machine-readable and interoperable through standardized semantic technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46a782dfec4ed85a41291a31e4dcf6cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe22bfea47113bef8076ac67e7587b69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa79759ff02333ae3d3a1d802134a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Emotion Intensity Prediction">
      <data key="d0">Emotion Intensity Prediction</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Emotion Intensity Prediction is a subfield of sentiment analysis and natural language processing focused on quantifying degrees of specific emotions such as anger, joy, fear, and sadness in textual data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe22bfea47113bef8076ac67e7587b69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intra-Sentence Attention RNN">
      <data key="d0">Intra-Sentence Attention RNN</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep learning architecture developed for the WASSA-2017 Shared Task that leverages token-level attention weights and pre-trained embeddings to predict emotion intensity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe22bfea47113bef8076ac67e7587b69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recurrent Neural Network">
      <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Network</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) is a class of artificial neural networks that computes word hidden states summarizing preceding words in sequential text data.&lt;SEP&gt;A category of neural networks designed to model sequential text data, applied in relation classification.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, referenced in the text in the form of LSTM RNN language models.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, utilized extensively in language modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, utilized for modeling event sequences and sequence-to-sequence event prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, utilized in text encoders, decoders, and reader models.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks possessing cyclic connections designed for sequential data processing, susceptible to vanishing and exploding gradient problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks specialized for processing sequential data, utilized to predict subsequent words in language modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks suited for sequential data processing, used in encoder-decoder setups for dialogue generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks suited for sequential data, utilized in both the encoder and decoder components of NMT systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of artificial neural networks that process sequential data by updating internal hidden state vectors recurrently across time steps, suitable for natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep neural network architectures with sequential memory, used in state-of-the-art dialogue state tracking models such as GLAD.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures designed for processing sequential data, used within the G-SAT encoder module to encode dialogue inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of neural network architectures designed to process sequential data by maintaining an internal hidden state recurrently updated across time steps.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network family (RNN) whose hidden unit dimensions (50, 100, 200) were evaluated for modeling sentence sequences in emotion intensity tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) is a class of artificial neural networks designed for sequential data processing, often augmented with attention models.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN) are sequential neural network architectures used as baseline systems and comparative models (such as RNN-based concat22 and s-hier variants) in the study.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b98e14081bd42f130f547ac6df8114f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57acb1a29c2b86c001f999352f15c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdef2f67b0ab332d8da79c41fb0e58c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab274e4799f62f2fbfabf369fb71267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1e71821eb167dabc5002a21237f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b6673cfdbb7f8a448709da4e46192b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8ad7bf1880d82f40811c2078046e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785a16b34b0c74a5ee4f9f416976a683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626602288681ee562ad75771b687c6be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4f52a592e1970d14c92e285c600305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9d3fbec1ae6ff5c0cac8214c21ddda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6c6ba3246066dafb17ed3cbf673534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe22bfea47113bef8076ac67e7587b69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GloVe">
      <data key="d0">GloVe</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pre-trained word representation model providing 100-dimensional vectors used to initialize word embedding layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained word representation model that provides dense vector embeddings used to initialize the word representations of actors, predicates, and objects.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of pre-trained word embeddings/vectors utilized to initialize word representations in the lookup table.&lt;SEP&gt;An unsupervised learning algorithm and pre-trained vector representation model trained on global word-word co-occurrence statistics from a text corpus.&lt;SEP&gt;An unsupervised word representation model providing pre-trained embeddings of dimensions 25, 50, and 100 tested across the emotion intensity benchmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;GloVe (Global Vectors for word representation) is an unsupervised deep learning approach for obtaining vector representations of words from text corpora.&lt;SEP&gt;GloVe is a pre-trained word embedding model utilized for sentence representation and semantic similarity comparisons across multiple benchmark tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;GloVe is an unsupervised pre-trained word representation model providing word embeddings evaluated as inputs to the WSD neural networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a8fecfb2a0e52c8eb6b888c9cbd44d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f22646227380376cc403c82c1f4615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626602288681ee562ad75771b687c6be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e48f19d4562e9a96fc6f5a1a6f337890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2a718261409ed817eb2c8548c15249f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe22bfea47113bef8076ac67e7587b69</data>
    </node>
