    <node id="BERT">
      <data key="d0">BERT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A bidirectional transformer language model trained on large-scale unsupervised corpora that achieves state-of-the-art performance across various natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of large pre-trained transformer language models targeted by various model compression and acceleration techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A language representation model built on the Transformer architecture designed to leverage unlabeled text data.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained contextualized language representation model category utilized for joint utterance-table schema encoding.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained neural language model architecture utilized within the utterance-table encoder to jointly encode user utterances and database column headers.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained transformer-based language model architecture consisting of embedding, encoder, and classification layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained transformer-based language model architecture that serves as the foundation and baseline for various downstream models and compression techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained transformer-based language model whose architecture and parameters serve as the foundation for the STR-encoder.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-trained transformer-based language representation model employed as a baseline and an arbitrator in the experimental framework.&lt;SEP&gt;A prominent category of transformer-based pre-trained language models adapted in the study as a shared parameter layer for joint learning.&lt;SEP&gt;A transformer-based language representation model architecture category used as a structural basis for the arbitrator module.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a category of pre-trained transformer language model known for its strong feature extraction capabilities, utilized as a base structure for downstream NLP tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a category of pretrained contextualized language representation models utilized to encode concatenated sequences of user utterances and database column headers.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a pre-trained bidirectional transformer language representation model whose parameters and feature extraction capabilities are leveraged in the proposed architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a pre-trained language model architecture whose self-attention encoder and structure serve as the foundation for the proposed shared task representation encoder.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a pre-trained masked language model used both as a target text classifier and as a generator for token replacements and insertions in adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a pre-trained transformer masked language model and classifier used both to generate adversarial mask perturbations and as a target classification model.&lt;SEP&gt;BERT is a pre-trained transformer-based language model architecture widely used in natural language processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers, a deep language model utilizing the Transformer encoder for self-supervised representation learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-56c893ccea72c9785303bae311f29c7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0003df2b872764693025524cf2fd334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1fb2eeb8c8333a70050efefb9412104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e33b95f1377956f09b6af9eda02260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15b5829d32b6817e2c4e142dba61455b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e97e9e342e051e03614c8dcaa59a2bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53d4fc8498b22f926c2a8c3d0057326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6907deaed642269724a32b0c9ccd9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb0afdde0d066987770f69fd6c4b0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9fdc4a98dc4d2c8f6875739e4d466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57acb1a29c2b86c001f999352f15c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e059280feab7e800ee2d2e025bc7cbd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LadaBERT">
      <data key="d0">LadaBERT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A BERT-oriented model compression approach that achieves superior performance and faster training speed across multiple compression ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight BERT model compression framework and model family that combines SVD-based matrix factorization, weight pruning, and knowledge distillation.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight adaptation framework for BERT that applies hybrid compression and knowledge distillation to create compact models.&lt;SEP&gt;A model compression framework that combines SVD-based matrix factorization, weight pruning, and multi-level knowledge distillation to achieve varying parameter reduction ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;LadaBERT is a lightweight model compression pipeline that creates adaptive BERT models using matrix factorization, weight pruning, and knowledge distillation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT-PKD">
      <data key="d0">BERT-PKD</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A BERT compression baseline model outperformed by LadaBERT-1 under a 2.5x compression ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;A BERT compression baseline that initializes a student model by selecting specific layers from a pre-trained BERT-Base teacher model.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient Knowledge Distillation, a model compression baseline extracting knowledge from intermediate Transformer layers into a 3-layer student model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TinyBERT">
      <data key="d0">TinyBERT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A compact student Transformer model comprising 14.5M parameters across 4 layers, utilized as a baseline and as the basis for multi-level distillation constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;A compressed BERT baseline model that relies on pure knowledge distillation from scratch and data augmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;A compressed BERT model framework that employs knowledge distillation constraints on embedding and intermediate layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A state-of-the-art BERT compression baseline outperformed by LadaBERT-3 under a 7.5x compression ratio.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Singular Value Decomposition (SVD)">
      <data key="d0">Singular Value Decomposition (SVD)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A widely used matrix factorization method that generalizes eigendecomposition to provide the optimal low-rank matrix approximation under the Frobenius norm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Acoustic Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Acoustic Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A discipline within speech processing that models relationships between audio signals and phonetic units using deep neural networks.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain in speech processing where deep neural network layers are compressed using low-rank matrix factorization and singular value decomposition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Text Classification">
      <data key="d0">Text Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental Natural Language Processing task that involves assigning predefined categories or labels to input text sequences or documents.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental natural language processing task category focused on assigning predefined labels or categories to text sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental natural language processing task that involves assigning predefined categories or labels to open-ended text.&lt;SEP&gt;A machine learning task formulation involving predicting discrete labels from input text sequences, used as a baseline framing for dialogue action prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task aimed at categorizing text sequences into discrete predicted class distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task that categorizes text, applied within dialogue systems for tasks such as emotion recognition and turn-taking arbitration.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task where word embedding layers are compressed using low-rank matrix factorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Text Classification is a general category of NLP tasks that involves categorizing text into predefined classes or labels.&lt;SEP&gt;Text Classification is a natural language processing task focused on categorizing text inputs, serving as the primary evaluation target for adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Text classification is a core natural language processing task category focused on assigning predefined labels or categories to text sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Text classification is a foundational natural language processing category focused on assigning predefined labels or categories to text documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Text classification is an NLP task performed directly from raw character sequences using convolutional neural networks by Zhang et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Text classification is an automated natural language processing task that assigns predefined labels or categories to text documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4524baad525e91d77888428268a1920e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53d4fc8498b22f926c2a8c3d0057326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a3ad946a112f7d6ba66cf07c1458d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6907deaed642269724a32b0c9ccd9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3a4a211bb43ab387afa7488082157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f148e57eed21f7948ba04d2d12e56d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784f828261b96cc3c6df35aff5b1cae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f43d3218257ab88ccde621eadece2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f5016d3aa81277cabc5c947f1ca64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sparsity-Induced Models">
      <data key="d0">Sparsity-Induced Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of neural network models that encourage zero-valued parameters during training using regularizers like group lasso and L0 regularization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binarized Neural Networks">
      <data key="d0">Binarized Neural Networks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An extreme class of quantized neural networks containing 1-bit binary weights and activations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Incremental Network Quantization">
      <data key="d0">Incremental Network Quantization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A weight quantization technique that converts full-precision models into low-precision networks via weight partitioning, groupwise quantization, and retraining.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Variational Network Quantization">
      <data key="d0">Variational Network Quantization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A weight quantization approach that formulates neural network parameter precision reduction as a variational inference problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GroupReduce">
      <data key="d0">GroupReduce</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A neural language model compression technique that applies low-rank matrix approximation to vocabulary partitions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7655d654b459dfdba7d9c1f562898a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Choi et al.">
      <data key="d0">Choi et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers who investigated the drawbacks of conventional k-means quantization methods and proposed a Hessian-weighted k-means clustering algorithm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chen et al.">
      <data key="d0">Chen et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Chen et al. refers to researchers who proposed a method for generating sense embeddings utilized to represent words and contexts in a shared vector space.&lt;SEP&gt;Researchers who applied knowledge distillation to object detection tasks using modified loss functions and adaptation layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Li et al.">
      <data key="d0">Li et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A research team that in 2017 introduced adversarial training for open-domain dialogue generation combining reinforcement learning and generative adversarial networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Researchers who developed frameworks leveraging knowledge distillation for learning from noisy labels and compressed DNN-based acoustic models using distillation and pruning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec69fa32e36eccb757533f339939eb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Anil et al.">
      <data key="d0">Anil et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers who proposed online distillation to enable extra parallelism when training large-scale data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Han et al.">
      <data key="d0">Han et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers who combined quantization, hamming coding, and weight pruning for model compression on image classification tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Yu et al.">
      <data key="d0">Yu et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers who proposed a unified framework for low-rank and sparse decomposition of weight matrices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Polino et al.">
      <data key="d0">Polino et al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers who advocated combining distillation and quantization, introducing quantified distillation and differentiable quantization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Network Quantization">
      <data key="d0">Network Quantization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A neural network compression technique that reduces the bit-width and precision of weights or activations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hybrid Model Compression">
      <data key="d0">Hybrid Model Compression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An approach that integrates multiple distinct compression techniques, such as pruning, quantization, and distillation, for enhanced efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Variational Inference">
      <data key="d0">Variational Inference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A statistical and machine learning framework that approximates complex probability densities, applied to network quantization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="K-Means Clustering">
      <data key="d0">K-Means Clustering</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An unsupervised clustering algorithm used in conventional quantization methods to group neural network weights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Object Detection">
      <data key="d0">Object Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A computer vision task focused on identifying and locating instances of semantic objects within digital images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Online Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Online Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A variant of knowledge distillation that trains multiple models simultaneously, enabling enhanced parallelism for large-scale data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Image Classification">
      <data key="d0">Image Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A core computer vision category involving the categorization of whole images into predefined classes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sparse Decomposition">
      <data key="d0">Sparse Decomposition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical decomposition technique that breaks down matrices into sparse components to reduce computational complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AutoML">
      <data key="d0">AutoML</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Automated Machine Learning, a field focused on automating the process of applying machine learning, including search for optimal model compression pipelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of machine learning paradigms focused on training decision-making agents through interactions within simulated environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A machine learning paradigm explored in dialogue systems to optimize conversational policies and agent interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A machine learning paradigm referenced as a baseline optimization technique alongside reward rescaling in coreference resolution tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A machine learning paradigm where an agent learns decision-making strategies through reward feedback, applied in compression pipelines to search configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;A machine learning paradigm where an agent learns to make decisions by receiving rewards, applied in open-domain dialogue generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement Learning is a machine learning paradigm used to directly optimize non-differentiable evaluation metrics, compared against differentiable relaxations.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement learning is a machine learning paradigm utilizing action-value functions and critic networks to optimize policy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement learning is an area of machine learning centered on trial-and-error strategy optimization, which is supported by the HoME platform.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90319301f543fcb7182148725008750f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b23b9abc552137b6cbb1c4cd6b7ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2425a9bfa1c48f3e56350fa213bdbdab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70218d643d3a2f540abe4bb2afd6986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6e4431e2ead79e10a12d16d49f4d480&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a61fcfaa9d7ad4a6f8c3cbb5352049c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Patient Knowledge Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Patient Knowledge Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specialized knowledge distillation methodology that extracts rich feature representations across intermediate hidden layers of teacher networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Singular Value Decomposition">
      <data key="d0">Singular Value Decomposition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A linear algebra factorization method that decomposes a parameter matrix into constituent singular vectors and values for low-rank compression.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical decomposition method, commonly known as SVD, used to perform low-rank matrix approximation for model parameter compression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Augmentation">
      <data key="d0">Data Augmentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A machine learning technique used to expand training data and mitigate model bias in neural relation extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique for expanding training samples, utilized in distillation pipelines such as TinyBERT.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used during distillation by models like TinyBERT to artificially expand training data in order to mimic teacher behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used to increase the diversity of training data by creating modified copies of existing data, employed in two-stage distillation pipelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-362346ad5b3a18dced3a68b0e282ea62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69bdb2043fb72d1301a9087fb8f43b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hybrid Compression">
      <data key="d0">Hybrid Compression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A model compression technique that integrates weight pruning directly onto low-rank decomposed matrices produced by SVD.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Low-Rank Matrix Approximation">
      <data key="d0">Low-Rank Matrix Approximation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical approximation technique that models a high-dimensional matrix by decomposing it into lower-rank representations via truncated singular value decomposition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT Encoder">
      <data key="d0">BERT Encoder</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A core structural component of the BERT model consisting of multiple transformer encoder layers subjected to hybrid compression in LadaBERT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Embedding Layer">
      <data key="d0">Embedding Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Embedding layer converts input word sequences into initial vector representations (H_0) prior to processing by attention layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The input representation layer of neural language models such as BERT, which is compressed using specified compression ratios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Classification Layer">
      <data key="d0">Classification Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A downstream task layer in BERT architectures, typically structured as a Multilayer Perceptron with Softmax activation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Teacher Model">
      <data key="d0">Teacher Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A full-sized or high-capacity neural network model used to guide and supervise smaller networks during knowledge distillation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Student Model">
      <data key="d0">Student Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A compact or compressed neural network model trained to mimic the intermediate outputs and representations of a teacher model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multilayer Perceptron">
      <data key="d0">Multilayer Perceptron</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Multilayer Perceptron (MLP) is a category of feedforward artificial neural network employed in the RC downstream task layer to map sequence representations to relation probability distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;A feedforward artificial neural network architecture commonly employed with Softmax activation in classification layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A feedforward artificial neural network class used as part of the classifier architecture with a sigmoid activation function.&lt;SEP&gt;Multilayer Perceptron is a feedforward artificial neural network model used to predict event spans and event attributes from learned features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-26c91c9a531d8aea5394e79e584448ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db96a568a81e93ae0f5b620a7d452203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e059280feab7e800ee2d2e025bc7cbd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Random Search">
      <data key="d0">Random Search</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A hyper-parameter search method applied to determine optimal fine-grained compression ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;An optimization algorithm used to explore and identify optimal fine-grained compression ratios across model layers using validation data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f56a06d096f62c8282f59e57d190e7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Embedding-Layer Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Embedding-Layer Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific knowledge distillation constraint applied to align the embedding layer representations between student and teacher models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Attention-Layer Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Attention-Layer Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A knowledge distillation technique that constrains the self-attention matrices of a student model to match those of a teacher model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hidden-Layer Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Hidden-Layer Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A knowledge distillation constraint enforcing alignment across intermediate fully-connected sub-layers in Transformer models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prediction-Layer Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Prediction-Layer Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The standard form of knowledge distillation using soft cross-entropy loss over output logits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hybrid Pruning">
      <data key="d0">Hybrid Pruning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A model compression approach combining SVD-based matrix factorization and iterative weight pruning.&lt;SEP&gt;A model compression technique that performs weight pruning on SVD-decomposed matrices, combining low-rank factorization and sparsity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentiment Classification">
      <data key="d0">Sentiment Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A machine learning task and methodology used to detect and predict sentiment from labeled and unlabeled social media texts across domains and languages.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language understanding task category evaluating text sentiment, exemplified by the SST-2 benchmark.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment Classification is a machine learning and natural language processing task aimed at categorizing text units into discrete sentiment classes such as negative, neutral, or positive.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment Classification is a machine learning task aimed at categorizing text into sentiment classes such as positive, negative, and neutral.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment Classification is an automated text classification category focusing on identifying the emotional polarity or subjective tone of texts such as Twitter posts.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment classification is a broad natural language processing category focused on analyzing and predicting affective states or polarities expressed in text.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment classification is a natural language processing task category focused on classifying the sentiment polarity of texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentiment classification is a subcategory of text classification focused on determining subjective attitudes or opinions in texts, evaluated on benchmarks like SST, IMDB, and MDSD.&lt;SEP&gt;The natural language processing task of categorizing text into sentiment classes, specifically ordered categories such as negative, neutral, and positive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f37521f7c9c4230a9fe0c9f8b7f1604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6c58bb9dd0e817dbe019ee67fada1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3194fa4581f2aaec823530e030775b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e33b95f1377956f09b6af9eda02260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b6bd8ee29f5ff509c2fa42f7d1d1739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b53c4d2b0ae2737239adca2c184b25d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f5016d3aa81277cabc5c947f1ca64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Language Inference">
      <data key="d0">Natural Language Inference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification task category determining inferential relationships between sentence pairs, such as MNLI and QNLI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pairwise Semantic Equivalence">
      <data key="d0">Pairwise Semantic Equivalence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of natural language tasks that assesses whether two sentences share identical meaning, such as QQP.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transformer Architectures">
      <data key="d0">Transformer Architectures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of deep learning neural network architectures relying on self-attention mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUE-Benchmark Evaluation Platform">
      <data key="d0">GLUE-Benchmark Evaluation Platform</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation benchmark platform and service used by the NLP community to assess and rank language models across diverse understanding tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT-Base">
      <data key="d0">BERT-Base</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A 12-layer pre-trained transformer model serving as the teacher model for distillation and compression baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;The pre-trained base Transformer checkpoint with 12 layers, 12 heads, 768 hidden units, and 110M parameters used as the initial model for compression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT-FT">
      <data key="d0">BERT-FT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline approach that directly fine-tunes BERT via supervision task labels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT-KD">
      <data key="d0">BERT-KD</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline compression approach implementing vanilla knowledge distillation on BERT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERT-SMALL">
      <data key="d0">BERT-SMALL</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline Transformer model with the same architecture as TinyBERT, pre-trained directly via the official BERT pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;A small-scale BERT model pre-trained from scratch on a smaller architecture using the official BERT pipeline.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distilled-BiLSTM">
      <data key="d0">Distilled-BiLSTM</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline model that distills knowledge into a single-layer bidirectional LSTM achieving a 10.8x compression ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;A distilled bidirectional LSTM recurrent model used as a baseline for model compression on natural language processing tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SST-2">
      <data key="d0">SST-2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark dataset used for evaluating sentiment classification in natural language understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;A binary sentiment classification benchmark dataset of movie reviews evaluated in the multi-cardinality multi-task scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;The Stanford Sentiment Treebank dataset used to evaluate sentiment classification performance in natural language processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784f828261b96cc3c6df35aff5b1cae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNLI">
      <data key="d0">MNLI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Multi-Genre Natural Language Inference dataset, evaluated across matched and mismatched settings (MNLI-m and MNLI-mm).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QNLI">
      <data key="d0">QNLI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A public question natural language inference dataset evaluated within natural language understanding benchmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Question-answering Natural Language Inference benchmark dataset used for language understanding evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QQP">
      <data key="d0">QQP</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Quora Question Pairs benchmark dataset used to evaluate semantic equivalence and sentence-pair classification.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quora Question Pairs dataset, used to evaluate models on pairwise semantic equivalence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SVD-Based Matrix Factorization">
      <data key="d0">SVD-Based Matrix Factorization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A low-rank matrix approximation method based on Singular Value Decomposition used to factorize weight matrices.&lt;SEP&gt;A low-rank matrix decomposition technique used to reduce parameters in neural network weight matrices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mean Squared Error">
      <data key="d0">Mean Squared Error</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A loss function adopted to compute distillation loss at the embedding, self-attention, and hidden representation layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical metric used to measure agreement on polarity ratings by penalizing larger numerical discrepancies between annotators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f74fa75c4a6b2b3f3b953b4f392d8136&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Soft Cross-Entropy Loss">
      <data key="d0">Soft Cross-Entropy Loss</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A loss function applied in prediction-layer distillation between the predictive logits of teacher and student models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BertAdam">
      <data key="d0">BertAdam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An optimization algorithm configured with default settings to optimize LadaBERT models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4f9917b54f845e14e0e4edafd46cb2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LadaBERT-1">
      <data key="d0">LadaBERT-1</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A compressed variant of LadaBERT with a 2.5x parameter reduction ratio, evaluated against BERT-PKD.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LadaBERT-3">
      <data key="d0">LadaBERT-3</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A compressed variant of LadaBERT with a 7.5x compression ratio, evaluated against TinyBERT and BERT-SMALL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LadaBERT-4">
      <data key="d0">LadaBERT-4</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A highly compressed variant of LadaBERT with high compression ratio, evaluated against Distilled-BiLSTM.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNLI-m">
      <data key="d0">MNLI-m</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A matched natural language inference benchmark dataset used to evaluate model accuracy and convergence speed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNLI-mm">
      <data key="d0">MNLI-mm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mismatched natural language inference benchmark dataset used for evaluating cross-domain model generalization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transformer">
      <data key="d0">Transformer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of neural network architecture implemented with multi-head attention and stacked layers in the seq2seq automation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture based entirely on self-attention mechanisms, used across various NLP tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture based on self-attention mechanisms, serving as the foundational building block for language models like BERT.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture based solely on attention mechanisms that achieves strong performance across numerous natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture category based on self-attention mechanisms, used as a foundation for context-aware machine translation models.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture using self-attention mechanisms, exhibiting faster inference than recurrent models of similar size.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network model architecture category utilizing self-attention mechanisms that outperformed ConvS2S across evaluated translation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A self-attention-based neural network architecture category evaluated for its superior performance and inference stability in speech act identification.&lt;SEP&gt;A state-of-the-art neural network architecture relying on self-attention mechanisms, trained and evaluated for translating English into South African languages.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transformer is a neural network architecture based on self-attention mechanisms, evaluated in context-aware translation experiments for its performance on intra-segmental and source-context pronoun translation.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformer is a neural machine translation architecture implemented using Tensor2Tensor that outperformed ConvS2S across all tested languages.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformer is a neural network architecture based on self-attention mechanisms, used in machine translation and language representations like BERT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9fdc4a98dc4d2c8f6875739e4d466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6907deaed642269724a32b0c9ccd9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddef736560bcb899db81b75205f4df60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0d62f131549ff6e8a1545f667c733a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f148e57eed21f7948ba04d2d12e56d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f50b15c876beec2eae8bf6437e8409aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24fec6e6dba96ab2ffdd4b5fac402b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2d07efa6f5f4a54b6cbbdd93f071bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BiLSTM">
      <data key="d0">BiLSTM</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A bidirectional long short-term memory recurrent neural network architecture implemented for sentence segmentation in obituaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A bidirectional recurrent neural network architecture comprising forward and backward LSTM components, used to learn sentence representations of event intents.&lt;SEP&gt;A bidirectional recurrent neural network architecture whose inference speed is typically slower than transformer-based architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory network, a type of recurrent neural network architecture used to determine the importance of segments in text inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f0f311662379cfa30789a001aeb981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be334478ba316675f89bc24ce6e3c03a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SVD Pruning">
      <data key="d0">SVD Pruning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A model reduction technique using Singular Value Decomposition matrix factorization to compress neural network weights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computer Vision">
      <data key="d0">Computer Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A field of artificial intelligence where complementary benefits of low-rank factorization and sparsity were previously demonstrated.&lt;SEP&gt;A subfield of artificial intelligence used to analyze meal images, identify ingredients, estimate volume, and assess nutritional content.&lt;SEP&gt;Computer Vision is a domain of artificial intelligence focused on extracting meaningful information from digital images and visual inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Computer Vision is a domain of artificial intelligence that extracts insights, patterns, and features from digital images.&lt;SEP&gt;Computer Vision is a domain of artificial intelligence where adversarial attacks were historically easier due to continuous input spaces compared to NLP.&lt;SEP&gt;Computer vision is a field of artificial intelligence focused on enabling computers to derive meaningful information from digital images, videos, and visual inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6482c4aa158143b58b33b61435191e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53d4fc8498b22f926c2a8c3d0057326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f1d3da436f9f4b7eadca13b0e5803e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae1796dede39736a6ce61ec4cb1e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fff775482c4d8a3088b428b10d9f761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d0">European Central Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Central Bank is an international financial institution cited as an antecedent example in sentence translation tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Context-Aware Translation">
      <data key="d0">Context-Aware Translation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Context-aware translation is a paradigm in machine translation that leverages inter-sentential context beyond single-sentence boundaries to improve translation coherence and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pronoun Translation">
      <data key="d0">Pronoun Translation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A linguistic phenomenon and evaluation focus in machine translation that often requires inter-sentential context to resolve correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized subfield and challenge within machine translation focusing on correctly resolving and translating anaphora across languages.&lt;SEP&gt;Pronoun translation is a machine translation challenge involving mapping pronouns such as English 'it' into gender-marked pronouns like German 'er', 'sie', or 'es'.&lt;SEP&gt;Pronoun translation is a specialized task and challenge in machine translation that frequently requires cross-sentence context to resolve gender, number, and antecedent ambiguities.&lt;SEP&gt;Pronoun translation is a specific linguistic challenge and evaluation task in machine translation concerning the correct translation of pronouns such as English 'it' into target language gendered forms like German 'er', 'sie', and 'es'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNLI-m Dataset">
      <data key="d0">MNLI-m Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">MNLI-m is a natural language inference benchmark dataset used to evaluate the accuracy and learning performance of language models like LadaBERT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QQP Dataset">
      <data key="d0">QQP Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">QQP (Quora Question Pairs) is a benchmark dataset used to evaluate the learning curve and performance of compressed language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLEU">
      <data key="d0">BLEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of standard evaluation metric for translation and text generation tasks, noted for potentially penalizing expressive diversity.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard automated evaluation metric used to calculate the linguistic quality and overlap of machine translation outputs against reference translations.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard evaluation metric that calculates n-gram precision to evaluate machine translation quality against reference translations.&lt;SEP&gt;A standardized automatic evaluation metric used in machine translation to assess the quality of translated text against reference translations.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated evaluation metric category used in natural language processing to assess the quality of machine translations.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated metric used to evaluate machine translation quality across test sets like newstest2017 and newstest2018.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU (Bilingual Evaluation Understudy) is an automatic evaluation metric that measures n-gram precision overlap between generated text segments and gold-standard references.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a quantitative evaluation metric used to benchmark and compare the translation accuracy of the machine translation models.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a standard automated evaluation metric used in machine translation to assess document- and sentence-level translation quality against reference translations.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a standard automated evaluation metric used in machine translation to assess overall translation quality, showing moderate improvements for context-aware models.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a standard evaluation metric in natural language processing used to measure the quality of machine-translated text against reference translations.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a standard evaluation metric used in natural language processing and machine translation to assess text generation quality.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is a standard evaluation metric used to score machine translation accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;BLEU is an evaluation metric commonly used to assess the quality of machine translation outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bilingual Evaluation Understudy (BLEU), an evaluation metric used to benchmark and measure translation quality in machine translation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Bilingual Evaluation Understudy, an automated evaluation metric used to assess the generation quality of the imaginator models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e97e9e342e051e03614c8dcaa59a2bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7818b9847aa576cb0d1559c6c5e963ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa612722a8775613a3ecb4a189613e3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddef736560bcb899db81b75205f4df60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0d62f131549ff6e8a1545f667c733a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acd45458d7c3c63e9891f23252405a17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70218d643d3a2f540abe4bb2afd6986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762be16cab89cb90aaf53d4505452bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cf9480461a20dfddfe7c1ed32cfa07c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad4815afd1a11fd7bc1c72c7da255e9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2d07efa6f5f4a54b6cbbdd93f071bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIBES">
      <data key="d0">RIBES</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">RIBES is an automated evaluation metric for machine translation designed to measure translation quality, particularly rank correlation of words.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sequence-to-Sequence Models">
      <data key="d0">Sequence-to-Sequence Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline class of neural network architectures commonly used for conversational agents and dialogue modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;An encoder-decoder neural network framework used to process variable-length input sequences into target sequences, widely used in translation, dialogue, and simplification.&lt;SEP&gt;Neural network architectures designed to map input sequences to output sequences, utilized in direct speech translation and speech recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sequence-to-sequence models are a class of neural network architectures commonly applied to tasks such as machine translation, summarization, and question answering.&lt;SEP&gt;Sequence-to-sequence models are an encoder-decoder neural network framework used to map input sequences to output sequences for generation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Sequence-to-sequence models are deep learning architectures designed to map an input sequence to an output sequence, commonly used in neural machine translation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f7cfb64157b0b1becf1f72e036758aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c10d3bd2a312359e6f2e1f854a8d2ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298f7bb76f5ebb6d2dd7ddc9afddde09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameter Tying">
      <data key="d0">Parameter Tying</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameter tying is a technique in neural architecture design where weights are shared across components, such as multi-encoder networks in context-aware translation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ff808f5f84391609fd609fe291c7f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DiscoMT">
      <data key="d0">DiscoMT</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">DiscoMT is an academic workshop series focusing on discourse in machine translation that hosts shared tasks such as pronoun prediction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WMT">
      <data key="d0">WMT</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">WMT is a premier machine translation conference and shared task competition that has co-hosted cross-lingual pronoun prediction tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-Lingual Pronoun Prediction Task">
      <data key="d0">Cross-Lingual Pronoun Prediction Task</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A shared evaluation task held at DiscoMT and WMT challenging participants to predict missing pronouns in target language translations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Context-Aware NMT">
      <data key="d0">Context-Aware NMT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of neural machine translation systems and architectures designed to incorporate information beyond single-sentence boundaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contrastive Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Contrastive Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation methodology assessing model accuracy based on whether the model scores correct reference translations higher than contrastive erroneous translations.&lt;SEP&gt;An evaluation methodology using targeted contrastive pairs to assess how accurately translation models handle specific linguistic phenomena like pronoun disambiguation.&lt;SEP&gt;Contrastive evaluation is an evaluation methodology in machine translation that tests a model's ability to discriminate between correct reference translations and contrastive incorrect variants by comparing model scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AutoPRF">
      <data key="d0">AutoPRF</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An automated reference-based evaluation metric that scores pronoun translation using word alignment between source, MT output, and reference translations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APT">
      <data key="d0">APT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An automated reference-based pronoun translation evaluation metric based on word alignment and pronoun identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OpenSubtitles Corpus">
      <data key="d0">OpenSubtitles Corpus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A large-scale multi-language subtitle dataset used to automatically extract contrastive examples for pronoun translation evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Encoder-Decoder Model">
      <data key="d0">Encoder-Decoder Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard sequence-to-sequence neural network architecture extended with additional context encoders and attention mechanisms for discourse modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Encoder-Decoder Model is a neural network architecture category that underpins sequence generation frameworks such as CopyRNN.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd9314a3266fc8d0bc21af4b765fa25b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Attention Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Attention Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep learning mechanism enabling models to dynamically focus on different parts of an input sequence, serving as the sole foundation of the Transformer architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;A deep learning technique that allows models to focus on specific parts of input sequences, foundational to modern dialogue models and Transformers.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network mechanism in the G-SAT classifier that weights the hidden states of input tokens to generate a slot-specific context vector.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network mechanism modified in context-aware architectures to allow models to attend to preceding context sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network mechanism within the encoder-decoder architecture that allows the decoder to access encoder states during translation.&lt;SEP&gt;An algorithmic component that allows the decoder in an NMT model to selectively focus on specific source representations from the encoder.&lt;SEP&gt;An attention mechanism is a neural network technique that dynamically assigns weights to relevant tokens or facts during inference and reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;An iterative neural scoring mechanism that computes attention weights over document tokens across multiple inference steps to guide answer prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Attention Mechanism is a deep learning technique that dynamically weights representations of different input segments to allow models to focus on relevant context and targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Attention Mechanism is a neural network component that dynamically weights and focuses on relevant features and token relationships within distributed representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b98e14081bd42f130f547ac6df8114f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1e71821eb167dabc5002a21237f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdef2f67b0ab332d8da79c41fb0e58c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7818b9847aa576cb0d1559c6c5e963ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2425a9bfa1c48f3e56350fa213bdbdab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6907deaed642269724a32b0c9ccd9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce525fd225c14101bb62983a2ac21a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f148e57eed21f7948ba04d2d12e56d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f43d3218257ab88ccde621eadece2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hierarchical Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Hierarchical Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multi-level neural network structure that uses cascaded RNNs to encode words into sentence vectors and combine them into document-level summaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inter-Sentential Anaphora">
      <data key="d0">Inter-Sentential Anaphora</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A linguistic discourse phenomenon where a pronoun refers to an antecedent located in a preceding sentence, requiring cross-sentence context to resolve.&lt;SEP&gt;Inter-sentential anaphora is a discourse-level linguistic phenomenon where a pronoun refers to an antecedent noun located across sentence boundaries in previous sentences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intra-Sentential Anaphora">
      <data key="d0">Intra-Sentential Anaphora</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A linguistic phenomenon where a pronoun and its antecedent exist within the same sentence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concatenation Technique">
      <data key="d0">Concatenation Technique</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A context-aware translation method that prepends preceding sentences directly to the current sentence without modifying model architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="German">
      <data key="d0">German</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A West Germanic language used in vector interpolation and cross-entropy evaluation alongside English.&lt;SEP&gt;A language category referenced in the context of the WMT 2014 translation benchmark for subword token optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;A major language possessing an aspect-annotated sentiment corpus, mentioned as an example of an adequately resourced language.&lt;SEP&gt;A parent language evaluated in transfer experiments for the Spanish-English child language pair, yielding lower Bleu scores than French.&lt;SEP&gt;German is a European language appearing as a false-positive language prediction within digital data sets for Russia.&lt;SEP&gt;German is a West Germanic language evaluated in cross-entropy interpolation experiments alongside English.&lt;SEP&gt;German is a language present in existing BLI evaluation dictionaries paired with English.&lt;SEP&gt;German is a natural language referenced as possessing rich morphological structures compared to English.&lt;SEP&gt;German is a natural language used in a German–English parent model to compare transfer performance against a French–English parent model.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the languages evaluated in the multilingual WOZ2.0 benchmark to measure the accuracy and prediction latency of dialogue state trackers.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the professional translation target languages evaluated in the multilingual WOZ2.0 dataset experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The target language chosen for evaluating difficult pronoun translation cases extracted from corpora.&lt;SEP&gt;The target language into which the WOZ2.0 dialogue benchmark was translated by professional translators for multilingual evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a29973c98d2c28f9d2efe87b89d1943f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1e71821eb167dabc5002a21237f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a0c631645254ecce4e14a53d44a991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7818b9847aa576cb0d1559c6c5e963ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7d53ab63937232bbcc4be9c7080dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9896f0582e2237c4a0dd8169f6817110&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1654ff6fd1aefc2ac7a0fb3a18a4eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c17cbdd46b3ef569862a8fa188b4fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6147035553ac26ef0837a5ab654f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785a16b34b0c74a5ee4f9f416976a683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2d07efa6f5f4a54b6cbbdd93f071bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebac0f3b43edbff22438f6ec756f16fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="French">
      <data key="d0">French</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Romance language analyzed in the study, noted for paradigm syncretism and large verbal paradigms.&lt;SEP&gt;A Romance language included in the bilingual dictionaries and extensively compared against MUSE baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-resource language paired with English to train the parent neural machine translation model.&lt;SEP&gt;A language category referenced in the context of the WMT 2014 subword token count benchmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;A parent language evaluated in transfer experiments, proving to be more effective than German for Spanish due to language similarity.&lt;SEP&gt;French is a Romance language evaluated in the study as part of the French–Spanish language pair.&lt;SEP&gt;French is a high-resource language used to train parent bilingual models for transfer learning into child models.&lt;SEP&gt;French is a major European language identified as an over-predicted false-positive language within digital datasets in Russia.&lt;SEP&gt;The high-resource natural language utilized as the source language for training the parent NMT model in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;The target language evaluated in the first edition of the cross-lingual pronoun prediction task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b98e14081bd42f130f547ac6df8114f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7818b9847aa576cb0d1559c6c5e963ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca3ab8f8c0dca0a40d79a8ee4226255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7d53ab63937232bbcc4be9c7080dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa31486ede85c18425009dc99542336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762be16cab89cb90aaf53d4505452bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c17cbdd46b3ef569862a8fa188b4fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00381e9f572e2f4c1655790b19b827fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a857415cf32d5d04b955b0da8d697209&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2d07efa6f5f4a54b6cbbdd93f071bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OpenSubtitles">
      <data key="d0">OpenSubtitles</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An online subtitle repository and project providing movie dialogue data used for question-answering sentence pairs to train neural models.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenSubtitles is an online platform for movie and television subtitles used as a data source mimicking informal speech for language identification training.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenSubtitles is an online subtitle platform and database from which a 12,000-instance contrastive test suite for pronoun translation was extracted.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenSubtitles is an online subtitle repository and project whose text corpus is used to extract English-German translation pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenSubtitles is an organization and resource provider whose subtitle corpus is used to extract dialogue question-answer pairs for natural language generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae11879a44e89506f5f7277c88df7c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b470fa40233ba7e36a9f7c70bafce9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coreference Resolution">
      <data key="d0">Coreference Resolution</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language processing task aimed at identifying when different mentions or expressions in a text refer to the same real-world entity.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task whose absence in the model causes classification errors in obituary sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference Resolution is a natural language processing task and clustering problem that identifies all mentions in a document referring to the same real-world entity.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference Resolution is a natural language processing task referenced as an area where gender bias evaluation and datasets have previously been developed.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference Resolution is a natural language processing task that involves determining whether different mentions or expressions in a text refer to the same entity.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference resolution is a natural language processing task aimed at identifying when different expressions in a text refer to the same entity.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference resolution is a natural language processing task that links pronouns to their corresponding antecedents within and across sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Coreference resolution is an NLP task and category focused on identifying mentions that refer to the same real-world entities in text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bac16ae7b48f68b81dcf01699b27c93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b23b9abc552137b6cbb1c4cd6b7ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2425a9bfa1c48f3e56350fa213bdbdab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70218d643d3a2f540abe4bb2afd6986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dddef9c6531f0d5588d28af861e6bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be334478ba316675f89bc24ce6e3c03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c71ebe855cec9ba2150fa3ef2be8c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Moses Tokenizer">
      <data key="d0">Moses Tokenizer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Moses tokenizer is a natural language processing tool used to tokenize text prior to alignment and parsing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fast_align">
      <data key="d0">Fast_align</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fast_align is an unsupervised word alignment tool used to generate symmetric word-level alignments between parallel texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast_align is an unsupervised word alignment tool used to generate token and pronoun alignments in the machine translation training dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CoreNLP">
      <data key="d0">CoreNLP</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CoreNLP is a natural language processing toolkit used to parse English sentences and perform neural coreference resolution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ParZu">
      <data key="d0">ParZu</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">ParZu is a dependency parsing tool used for syntactic analysis of German text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CorZu">
      <data key="d0">CorZu</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CorZu is a coreference resolution system designed for German text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parsing">
      <data key="d0">Parsing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A computational linguistic task involving analyzing the syntactic structure of sentences according to a formal grammar.&lt;SEP&gt;Parsing is a natural language processing task involving syntactic structural analysis, addressed by Ballesteros et al. using a character-level model.&lt;SEP&gt;Parsing is the computational syntactic analysis of sentence structures, providing part-of-speech and dependency information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd3a4a211bb43ab387afa7488082157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4117dfdbcf8427f9aa5d8d43444fb707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contrastive Translation">
      <data key="d0">Contrastive Translation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A contrastive translation is an artificially modified translation variant where a correct pronoun is replaced by an incorrect one to test system discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nominal Antecedent">
      <data key="d0">Nominal Antecedent</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A nominal antecedent is a noun or noun phrase in a coreference chain that provides the gender and referential context for a pronoun.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grammatical Gender Disambiguation">
      <data key="d0">Grammatical Gender Disambiguation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Grammatical gender disambiguation is the process of selecting the correct gendered pronoun in the target language based on the antecedent's gender.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f2d2324dc0fae4c7fa89a1690e31637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WMT 2017 English-to-German News Translation Shared Task">
      <data key="d0">WMT 2017 English-to-German News Translation Shared Task</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The WMT 2017 English-to-German news translation shared task is a competitive benchmark event providing training data of approximately 5.8 million sentence pairs for evaluating machine translation models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recurrent Models">
      <data key="d0">Recurrent Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of neural machine translation architectures based on recurrent neural networks (RNNs) with attention, tested with various context-aware and concatenation configurations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transformer Models">
      <data key="d0">Transformer Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of neural machine translation architectures that eschew recurrence in favor of stacked self-attention and fully connected feedforward layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Context-Aware Models">
      <data key="d0">Context-Aware Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Context-aware models are specialized neural machine translation architectures that incorporate inter-sentential context to improve coreference resolution and pronoun accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Neural machine translation architectures designed to incorporate preceding source or target sentence context to better resolve discourse phenomena.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence-Level NMT">
      <data key="d0">Sentence-Level NMT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standard baseline neural machine translation systems that translate sentences in isolation without access to surrounding cross-sentence context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nematus">
      <data key="d0">Nematus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A neural machine translation toolkit used to implement and train bidirectional recurrent neural network baselines and context-aware recurrent models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SacreBLEU">
      <data key="d0">SacreBLEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard evaluation tool used to compute BLEU scores to measure overall translation quality in machine translation experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adam">
      <data key="d0">Adam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An optimization algorithm used to train recurrent neural network models with an initial learning rate of 0.0001.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Byte Pair Encoding">
      <data key="d0">Byte Pair Encoding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A data compression algorithm adapted to learn subword translation units based on statistical properties and frequent character sequences in text.&lt;SEP&gt;A data-driven subword segmentation algorithm that iteratively merges the most frequent character bigrams.&lt;SEP&gt;A subword segmentation algorithm and representation unit evaluated for machine translation efficiency against words, morphemes, and syllables.&lt;SEP&gt;A subword segmentation algorithm applied to source and target texts to handle open vocabulary in both RNN and Transformer models.&lt;SEP&gt;A subword segmentation method and translation unit representation evaluated for machine translation between related languages.&lt;SEP&gt;A subword tokenization algorithm (BPE) analyzed in relation to machine translation performance and BLEU scores.&lt;SEP&gt;A subword tokenization technique (BPE) analyzed through an ablation study to find optimal token vocabularies across different language dataset sizes.&lt;SEP&gt;Byte Pair Encoding (BPE) is a data compression and subword segmentation technique used to address vocabulary limitations in neural language models.&lt;SEP&gt;Byte Pair Encoding (BPE) is a substitution dictionary-based subword segmentation algorithm widely used as a standard preprocessing method in neural machine translation.&lt;SEP&gt;Byte Pair Encoding (BPE) is a subword tokenization and representation technique that provides writing system independence and improves translation accuracy across various languages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea126b0da9c38f85b697b36cd33629f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3fa25c5e29c7ea3201eac4d5fbec61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e060c5bbcfa40d71aa9fb0a2e63bff30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acd45458d7c3c63e9891f23252405a17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f50b15c876beec2eae8bf6437e8409aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cf9480461a20dfddfe7c1ed32cfa07c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffaa7abbd8709e94a9523e6b922ac96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S-Hier-To-2">
      <data key="d0">S-Hier-To-2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A context-aware recurrent model that uses an additional encoder for source context and concatenates target context, achieving top performance in pronoun translation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S-Hier">
      <data key="d0">S-Hier</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multi-encoder recurrent architecture with hierarchical attention that incorporates the previous source sentence as context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S-T-Hier">
      <data key="d0">S-T-Hier</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multi-encoder recurrent model with hierarchical attention that reads both the previous source sentence and previous target sentence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concat22">
      <data key="d0">Concat22</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A contextual translation approach that concatenates each sentence with one preceding sentence on both the source and target sides.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concat21">
      <data key="d0">Concat21</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A contextual translation architecture where the preceding sentence is concatenated to the current sentence only on the source side.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Newstest2017">
      <data key="d0">Newstest2017</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard benchmark evaluation test set from the WMT 2017 news translation shared task used to measure BLEU scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Newstest2018">
      <data key="d0">Newstest2018</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard benchmark evaluation test set from WMT 2018 used to measure BLEU scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Weight Tying">
      <data key="d0">Weight Tying</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A parameter-sharing method where embedding matrices between encoders reading the same side of text share parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f00c8140006c06dd00e51d3d0d5296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Swiss National Science Foundation">
      <data key="d0">Swiss National Science Foundation</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Swiss National Science Foundation (SNF) is a research funding agency that provided financial support for the CoNTra research project under grant number 105212_169888.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WMT 2017">
      <data key="d0">WMT 2017</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The 2017 Conference on Machine Translation (WMT 2017) news translation task, which provided training data and test sets for machine translation models.&lt;SEP&gt;The WMT 2017 news translation task is a machine translation benchmark and shared task whose dataset was used to train the translation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CoNTra">
      <data key="d0">CoNTra</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CoNTra is a funded scientific research project focused on contrastive evaluation and machine translation, supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Encoder Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Encoder Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-encoder architecture is a neural model design strategy in context-aware translation that utilizes separate encoders for context and source sentences, outperforming simple concatenation approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameter Sharing">
      <data key="d0">Parameter Sharing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A joint learning mechanism that shares a feature extraction layer between named entity recognition and relation classification models.&lt;SEP&gt;Parameter sharing is a machine learning optimization technique where weights are tied between contextual and primary encoders or decoders, significantly boosting model accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-57acb1a29c2b86c001f999352f15c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coreference Chain">
      <data key="d0">Coreference Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A coreference chain is a sequence of referring expressions in discourse that refer to the same nominal entity across multiple sentences, providing contextual signals for translation models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contrastive Test Suite">
      <data key="d0">Contrastive Test Suite</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The contrastive test suite is a specialized machine translation benchmark comprising 12,000 test cases designed to evaluate whether neural models can correctly translate pronouns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="German Language">
      <data key="d0">German Language</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The German language is the target language in the translation experiments, presenting morphological gender distinctions in pronouns such as 'er', 'sie', and 'es'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="English Language">
      <data key="d0">English Language</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language used to present demonstrative example sentences and annotation schemes in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A widely researched Germanic language used as a baseline and comparison point for directive analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The English language is the source language in the experiments, characterized by gender-neutral third-person pronouns such as 'it'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-159ff4436a1c0b10a07d168b9d3ad6b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18770431e1f17cd9efc7aedcdb98d303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aa2405678391ab9324cffd6cdbbadc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FreeFollowers">
      <data key="d0">FreeFollowers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An online blackmarket service that allows users to gain inorganic appraisals and artificial engagement on social media platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Like4Like">
      <data key="d0">Like4Like</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A blackmarket service platform that facilitates artificial engagement and appraisals on social media.&lt;SEP&gt;Like4Like is an underground credit-based freemium blackmarket website crawled to collect data on collusive retweeting behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YouLikeHits">
      <data key="d0">YouLikeHits</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An online service that enables users to generate inorganic appraisals and engagement metrics for social media content.&lt;SEP&gt;YouLikeHits is an underground credit-based freemium blackmarket website used to gain retweets and other social media appraisals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JustRetweet">
      <data key="d0">JustRetweet</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A blackmarket service allowing users to submit tweets to obtain artificial retweets and endorsements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Blackmarket Tweets">
      <data key="d0">Blackmarket Tweets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of tweets submitted to blackmarket engagement services to gain artificially inflated retweets, likes, and reach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social Spam">
      <data key="d0">Social Spam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of fraudulent or unsolicited content and activity on social media platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NTra">
      <data key="d0">NTra</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A funding agency or project responsible for awarding grant number 105212_169888.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bots">
      <data key="d0">Bots</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Automated accounts on social networks studied in research focused on detecting fraudulent and automated behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fake Followers">
      <data key="d0">Fake Followers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Inauthentic or fabricated accounts used to artificially inflate user follower counts on social networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Collusive Retweeters">
      <data key="d0">Collusive Retweeters</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Coordinated groups of accounts that collaborate fraudulently to artificially amplify and retweet content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Spammers">
      <data key="d0">Spammers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Entities or users who generate unsolicited, repetitive, or deceptive social media content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Blackmarket Users">
      <data key="d0">Blackmarket Users</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Social media users who utilize blackmarket engagement services to gain inorganic appraisals and artificial reach for their posts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Genuine Tweets">
      <data key="d0">Genuine Tweets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legitimate, authentic tweets that are posted organically without relying on blackmarket amplification services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Blackmarket Services">
      <data key="d0">Blackmarket Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Blackmarket services are underground platforms and mechanisms where users collusively purchase or trade social media appraisals such as retweets.&lt;SEP&gt;Online platforms that offer inorganic social media engagement such as likes, retweets, and followers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content-Level Appraisals">
      <data key="d0">Content-Level Appraisals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Metrics and signals of support on Twitter, specifically including Likes, Retweets, and Quotes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07c99aac0aabed061997544b990b7004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Yardi">
      <data key="d0">Yardi</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Yardi is a researcher who studied the network structures of spammers and non-spammers and tracked endogenous Twitter content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chen">
      <data key="d0">Chen</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Chen is a researcher who conducted comprehensive evaluations of machine learning algorithms for timely spam detection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serrano">
      <data key="d0">Serrano</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Serrano is a researcher who conducted an extensive survey on fake tweet detection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Motoyama">
      <data key="d0">Motoyama</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Motoyama is a researcher who provided detailed analyses of underground forums and social network structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dutta">
      <data key="d0">Dutta</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dutta is a researcher who investigated customers involved in purchasing fake retweets and analyzed models of blackmarket services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chetan">
      <data key="d0">Chetan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Chetan is a researcher who proposed CoReRank and CoReRank+ to detect collusive users involved in retweeting activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Misra">
      <data key="d0">Misra</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Misra is a researcher who introduced Cross-Stitch units for multitask learning representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Zhang">
      <data key="d0">Zhang</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher investigating character-level models for natural language processing tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who, with Lapata, framed the encoder-decoder model as an agent using deep reinforcement learning for sentence simplification.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang is a researcher who classified multitask learning models into five distinct types.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang is a researcher who, along with colleagues, previously proposed a decoding approach for text simplification that this work contrasts with by implementing greedy and beam-search strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang is a researcher who, along with colleagues, trained a convolutional neural network to perform text classification directly from characters without using words.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4117dfdbcf8427f9aa5d8d43444fb707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab274e4799f62f2fbfabf369fb71267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3a4a211bb43ab387afa7488082157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298f7bb76f5ebb6d2dd7ddc9afddde09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Freemium Services">
      <data key="d0">Freemium Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Freemium services are a category of blackmarket services that provide both paid and unpaid options to earn appraisals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Premium Services">
      <data key="d0">Premium Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Premium services are a category of blackmarket services accessible only via monetary payment from customers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Credit-Based Services">
      <data key="d0">Credit-Based Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Credit-based services are a sub-category of freemium blackmarket services where users earn credits by appraising others' content to gain appraisals for their own.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social-Share Services">
      <data key="d0">Social-Share Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Social-share services are a sub-category of freemium blackmarket services that require customers to share content on social media.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Auto-Time Retweet Services">
      <data key="d0">Auto-Time Retweet Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Auto-Time retweet services are a sub-category of freemium blackmarket services that use Twitter access tokens to automatically retweet content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Promotional">
      <data key="d0">Promotional</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A topical category of tweets accounting for 23.29% of the false negatives in the tweet classification model.&lt;SEP&gt;A tweet category identifying tweets that attempt to promote a website, product, or service.&lt;SEP&gt;Promotional is an annotation category of tweets that attempt to market a website, product, or account.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fake Tweets">
      <data key="d0">Fake Tweets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fake tweets represent a category of malicious social media posts designed to spread misinformation, often linked to major events.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Spam">
      <data key="d0">Spam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A tweet classification category representing unwanted, deceptive, or automated messages commonly targeted in detection studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A tweet content category examined during classification robustness evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;Spam refers to malicious, unsolicited, or automated tweets and content detected on social platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IRB">
      <data key="d0">IRB</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Institutional Review Board, an administrative body that oversees and approves research involving human subjects to ensure ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Institutional Review Board (IRB) is an administrative body that reviewed and granted ethical approval for the researchers to create dummy accounts on blackmarket platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c029640c5730b975534572e9f8f96fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multitask Learning">
      <data key="d0">Multitask Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A machine learning paradigm adopted to jointly train the primary binary classification task and secondary engagement regression task.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitask learning is a machine learning paradigm used to simultaneously optimize two or more related tasks through shared representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Malicious Activities">
      <data key="d0">Malicious Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Malicious activities encompass harmful behaviors in social networks, specifically including spam, fake content, and blackmarket services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Major Events">
      <data key="d0">Major Events</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Major events are significant real-world occurrences during which accounts spreading fake tweets and misinformation are frequently created.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Entertainment">
      <data key="d0">Entertainment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A topical category of tweets accounting for 21.92% of the false negatives in the evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Entertainment is a topical category of blackmarket tweets comprising 15.89% of the annotated test dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="News">
      <data key="d0">News</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A tweet content category for which the proposed model demonstrates robust blackmarket classification performance.&lt;SEP&gt;News is a content category of blackmarket tweets accounting for 7.86% of the annotated test dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Politics">
      <data key="d0">Politics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general news categorization field found in the HTML pages of news articles.&lt;SEP&gt;A societal domain characterized by governance and public affairs, noted for being adversely impacted and polarized by the spread of fake news.&lt;SEP&gt;A topical category of tweets against which the classification model demonstrates robust detection performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Politics is a thematic category of blackmarket tweets accounting for 4.82% of the annotated test dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Politics is a thematic topic and domain category often represented in fake news research and datasets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6187c8bb0f977bcb9db2949d166fa2cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5179247480b7af630790fe26e5e9372c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-261a6f8ccfb17ebb9be72e74900d0a04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Others">
      <data key="d0">Others</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A residual classification category of tweets accounting for 28.77% of false negatives, noted as particularly difficult to distinguish from genuine tweets.&lt;SEP&gt;A tweet category largely encompassing personal tweets without explicit call to action, though potentially functioning as self-promotion.&lt;SEP&gt;Others is a residual annotation category representing 14.11% of blackmarket tweets, primarily consisting of personal and self-promotional posts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74441bc0683e1fe464f8cf5bd0c14d93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dhingra Et Al.">
      <data key="d0">Dhingra Et Al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dhingra et al. are researchers who provided the pre-trained Tweet2Vec model trained on a dataset of 2 million tweets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wu Et Al.">
      <data key="d0">Wu Et Al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Wu et al. are researchers who proposed a Twitter spam detection method using Word2Vec and Doc2Vec with an MLP classifier.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rajdev Et Al.">
      <data key="d0">Rajdev Et Al.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Rajdev et al. are researchers who proposed flat and hierarchical classification approaches to classify spam, fake, and legitimate tweets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Blackmarket">
      <data key="d0">Blackmarket</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification category representing tweets associated with blackmarket manipulation services or illicit promotion.&lt;SEP&gt;A target class in the binary classification task representing tweets submitted to blackmarket services for inorganic engagement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Genuine">
      <data key="d0">Genuine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification category representing legitimate or normal non-manipulated tweets.&lt;SEP&gt;A target class representing legitimate, authentic tweets in the binary classification problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Not-Spam">
      <data key="d0">Not-Spam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification category representing non-spam or authentic social media content used in baseline spam detection frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fake">
      <data key="d0">Fake</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category used in tweet classification setups to identify fraudulent or counterfeit social media posts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legitimate">
      <data key="d0">Legitimate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category denoting genuine and authentic social media posts within hierarchical and flat classification frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binary Classification">
      <data key="d0">Binary Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The machine learning task category utilized as the primary objective to differentiate tweets between blackmarket and genuine classes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regression">
      <data key="d0">Regression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of predictive modeling used as the secondary task to forecast numerical counts of likes and retweets after five days.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tweet Content Features">
      <data key="d0">Tweet Content Features</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A feature set category encompassing twelve content-based metrics including mentions, hashtags, URLs, sentiment scores, and linguistic counts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Random Forest">
      <data key="d0">Random Forest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An ensemble learning algorithm category used as a baseline classifier for tweet categorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Random Forest is an ensemble machine learning algorithm incorporated into baseline STS systems like ECNU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Layer Perceptron">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Layer Perceptron</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) is a feedforward artificial neural network used with one hidden layer in the compose function of Neural Semantic Encoders.&lt;SEP&gt;A feedforward artificial neural network classifier category utilized in baseline detection systems and feature evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-layer perceptron is an artificial neural network architecture trained with character trigrams to perform 464-language identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b470fa40233ba7e36a9f7c70bafce9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab274e4799f62f2fbfabf369fb71267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Support Vector Machine">
      <data key="d0">Support Vector Machine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Support Vector Machine (SVM) is a supervised machine learning classification algorithm utilized to determine tweet polarity.&lt;SEP&gt;A supervised learning model with associated learning algorithms that analyzes data for classification and regression in attribute extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;A supervised machine learning classification algorithm evaluated across different feature granularities.&lt;SEP&gt;A supervised machine learning classification algorithm utilized to determine tweet polarity.&lt;SEP&gt;A supervised machine learning model category used as a baseline classifier on combined tweet feature vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Support Vector Machine (SVM) is a supervised learning model used for pattern recognition and classification, utilized by systems like IRST-Kernels and nusels.&lt;SEP&gt;Support Vector Machine (SVM) is a supervised machine learning classifier used to classify sentiment in Twitter messages based on rich linguistic and lexicon features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31134945186e62e7effccb3ba89b180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e9f52662c01528fd8d607b1462c48df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e060c5bbcfa40d71aa9fb0a2e63bff30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289c3be854417f1af5a604180e6310cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76f1c0c2ed37a786263a6a6d8b0bb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8ba467b047874b47272d3f7da22302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DST">
      <data key="d0">DST</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">DST (Department of Science and Technology) is a funding body that provided financial support for the blackmarket tweet detection research under grant numbers ECR/2017/001691 and DST/INT/UK/P158/2017.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infosys Centre of AI">
      <data key="d0">Infosys Centre of AI</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An artificial intelligence research center based at IIIT-Delhi that partially funded the research project.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IIIT-Delhi">
      <data key="d0">IIIT-Delhi</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Indraprastha Institute of Information Technology Delhi, an academic institution hosting the Infosys Centre of AI in India.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="India">
      <data key="d0">India</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A country referenced in connection to regional languages and linguistic contact.&lt;SEP&gt;A country whose government bodies funded the translation research and whose languages were studied in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a country identified as significantly under-represented in both web-crawled and Twitter language datasets relative to its population size.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a country in South Asia characterized by rich linguistic diversity and related languages needing translation resources.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a country whose languages are targeted through corpora such as the Emille corpus and the Indian Parallel Corpus in the language identification project.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a country with over-predicted languages identified in the Twitter corpus.&lt;SEP&gt;India is the country in which the 2014 general elections analyzed in the research occurred.&lt;SEP&gt;India is the country where the 2014 general elections analyzed in the prediction dataset were held.&lt;SEP&gt;India is the sovereign nation where the 2014 general elections were held.&lt;SEP&gt;The country where IIIT-Delhi and the Infosys Centre of AI are located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea126b0da9c38f85b697b36cd33629f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7d53ab63937232bbcc4be9c7080dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b470fa40233ba7e36a9f7c70bafce9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a214a03aad6b4356ff5b17786166ad02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97953bb0d586e46165fea699da6cf781&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3fa25c5e29c7ea3201eac4d5fbec61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d721fe5dad0029252753a2c12969e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3643b20dc5e5b3d9faa14743574ec5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UK">
      <data key="d0">UK</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The United Kingdom, a nation where veterinary clinics contribute clinical documents to the VetCompass repository.&lt;SEP&gt;The United Kingdom, one of the geographical regions analyzed in the obituary classification study.&lt;SEP&gt;The United Kingdom, referenced in the international collaboration funding code DST/INT/UK/P158/2017.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c029640c5730b975534572e9f8f96fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9645cad08b5b060013cac117d156f888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SemEval">
      <data key="d0">SemEval</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An ongoing series of semantic evaluation workshops and competitive shared tasks in NLP, including benchmark tasks on aspect-level sentiment analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;An ongoing series of semantic evaluation workshops and shared tasks, providing datasets such as SICK for evaluating semantic textual similarity.&lt;SEP&gt;SemEval (Semantic Evaluation) is an ongoing series of computational linguistics evaluations and workshops, specifically referencing the 2013–2015 benchmark datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;SemEval (Semantic Evaluation) is an ongoing series of evaluations and workshops that provide benchmark datasets and challenges for natural language processing.&lt;SEP&gt;SemEval is an ongoing series of evaluations and workshops that provides benchmark datasets, tasks, and official evaluation scripts for natural language processing.&lt;SEP&gt;SemEval is an ongoing series of semantic evaluation workshops and competitive shared tasks, providing benchmark datasets such as SemEval13-16 for sentiment analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a29973c98d2c28f9d2efe87b89d1943f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b5684eaac7a3f52271bc1ff14d5ff1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3194fa4581f2aaec823530e030775b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b6bd8ee29f5ff509c2fa42f7d1d1739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67aef3e225567bceaa8ddbf5e9866527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ramanujan Fellowship">
      <data key="d0">Ramanujan Fellowship</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A scientific research fellowship and funding body in India that partially supported the research on blackmarket tweet identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Textual Similarity">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Textual Similarity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A central category of natural language processing tasks aimed at determining the degree of semantic equivalence between pairs of sentences or short texts.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing benchmark task (STS) focused on determining the degree of equivalence and similarity between sentence pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task (SICK-R / STS) evaluating the semantic equivalence between sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Textual Similarity (STS) is a natural language processing task and benchmark category that evaluates the degree of semantic equivalence between pairs of sentences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c10d3bd2a312359e6f2e1f854a8d2ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paraphrase Identification">
      <data key="d0">Paraphrase Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of NLP tasks focused on detecting whether two sentences express the exact same meaning using different expressions.&lt;SEP&gt;An NLP task focused on recognizing whether two sentences share equivalent semantic meanings.&lt;SEP&gt;Paraphrase Identification is a natural language processing category and task aimed at identifying whether two sentences convey the same meaning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dcb2d684d656e9d9c24124949d2aaf80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Textual Entailment">
      <data key="d0">Textual Entailment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of NLP language understanding tasks dedicated to determining whether a premise text entails or logically leads to a hypothesis text.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task (SICK-E) aimed at determining directional relationship between text fragments.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing task focused on determining whether a premise sentence entails a given hypothesis sentence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c10d3bd2a312359e6f2e1f854a8d2ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Plagiarism Detection">
      <data key="d0">Plagiarism Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An application category in natural language processing that relies on short-text semantic similarity metrics to identify copied or unoriginal text.&lt;SEP&gt;Plagiarism detection is the task of identifying uncredited copying or shared authorship in texts, highlighted as a complex task analogous to cross-network profile matching.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72431d36a16227ea7d1db8d40a9ca21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Question Answering">
      <data key="d0">Question Answering</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A computational task and application area where concise natural language summaries of facts are generated to answer user queries.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental natural language processing task aimed at automatically answering queries based on textual context.&lt;SEP&gt;A prominent natural language processing task and system domain focused on generating accurate answers to user queries.&lt;SEP&gt;A research field in Artificial Intelligence dedicated to designing intelligent systems that provide correct answers to user questions formulated in natural language.&lt;SEP&gt;An NLP application category in which semantic similarity and sentence modeling play a fundamental role in matching questions to answers.&lt;SEP&gt;An NLP sentence relation modeling task dedicated to automatically resolving questions posed in natural language.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering (QA) is a natural language processing task and system domain focused on generating accurate answers to user queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering (QA) is a research category within artificial intelligence and natural language processing focused on training models to comprehend queries and provide correct answers.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering (QA) is an NLP research area focusing on building neural and linguistic systems that map input questions directly to appropriate answers.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering (QA) is an NLP research task and system domain focused on automatically providing direct answers to natural language questions.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering is a computational NLP task focused on developing intelligent agents to provide relevant answers to user queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering is a natural language processing task aimed at automatically answering questions posed by users, which benefits from multi-step reasoning and coreference resolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Question Answering is an advanced application in the natural language processing pipeline that utilizes word sense disambiguation.&lt;SEP&gt;Question answering is a natural language processing task category where models extract or generate answers to queries, commonly utilizing multi-sentence segment embeddings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdef2f67b0ab332d8da79c41fb0e58c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2425a9bfa1c48f3e56350fa213bdbdab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcb2d684d656e9d9c24124949d2aaf80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7d53ab63937232bbcc4be9c7080dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b6bd8ee29f5ff509c2fa42f7d1d1739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f22646227380376cc403c82c1f4615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53d0ac7fa47d30ce6f399d3ef8b95e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152eae14a34b247b0c7628803502e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18770431e1f17cd9efc7aedcdb98d303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9c29cc7a5d0f200ae552bfc4494ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76f1c0c2ed37a786263a6a6d8b0bb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fff775482c4d8a3088b428b10d9f761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SemEval-2017">
      <data key="d0">SemEval-2017</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">SemEval-2017 is an international semantic evaluation workshop and competition where hybrid approaches and models competed on the Semantic Textual Similarity (STS) task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECNU">
      <data key="d0">ECNU</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ECNU refers to the East China Normal University team and system, which developed a state-of-the-art ensemble model for the STS Benchmark dataset at SemEval-2017.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Textual Entailment Recognition">
      <data key="d0">Textual Entailment Recognition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Textual Entailment Recognition is a natural language processing task that determines whether a given sentence logically entails, contradicts, or is neutral toward another sentence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Word Embedding">
      <data key="d0">Word Embedding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of distributed vector representations of words in natural language processing, often pre-trained and used as inputs for neural models.&lt;SEP&gt;A category of natural language processing techniques and models that map words to dense vectors in a continuous semantic space.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous vector representation of words capturing lexical and semantic relationships, used as fundamental building blocks in NLP models.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous, multi-dimensional vector representation assigned to each word token from a vocabulary and stored in an embedding matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;A representation technique where words are mapped to dense, continuous, fixed-length vectors containing semantic implications via a lookup table.&lt;SEP&gt;Word Embedding is a continuous vector space representation of words, used by baseline attack methods to measure token-level similarity.&lt;SEP&gt;Word Embedding is a feature representation technique that converts discrete word tokens into dense numerical vectors via lookup tables.&lt;SEP&gt;Word Embedding is a natural language processing technique for representing words as continuous vectors that capture semantic and syntactic information.&lt;SEP&gt;Word embedding is a continuous vector space representation capturing syntactic and semantic characteristics of words from text corpora.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53d4fc8498b22f926c2a8c3d0057326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4117dfdbcf8427f9aa5d8d43444fb707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f874c842ec2c36b07a6dd2abcb11dba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9d3fbec1ae6ff5c0cac8214c21ddda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c91c9a531d8aea5394e79e584448ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Convolutional Neural Network">
      <data key="d0">Convolutional Neural Network</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of deep learning architectures that uses convolutional filters to extract features from inputs such as pre-trained word embeddings.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep neural network architectures evaluated as a data-driven model for dialogue state tracking.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep neural network architectures that use convolutional layers to extract local features from input sequences or spatial data.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep neural networks commonly applied to analyze visual imagery and extract feature representations from images and text.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of deep neural networks used to extract local features for tasks like relation classification without manual feature engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;A deep learning architecture designed for feature extraction, applied by prior researchers in character recognition transfer experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network architecture applied to dialogue state tracking capable of achieving competitive performance without pre-trained embeddings.&lt;SEP&gt;Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a category of deep learning architecture that utilizes convolutional filters and pooling layers to capture local features and dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a class of deep neural networks commonly used to process grid or sequence data through learnable filter convolutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Convolutional neural networks are neural architectures used to derive word representations from character sequences and perform text classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b98e14081bd42f130f547ac6df8114f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76f1c0c2ed37a786263a6a6d8b0bb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57acb1a29c2b86c001f999352f15c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3a4a211bb43ab387afa7488082157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c91c9a531d8aea5394e79e584448ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45dd962c5b788395b9105c9472288d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6147035553ac26ef0837a5ab654f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Long Short Term Memory">
      <data key="d0">Long Short Term Memory</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An advanced recurrent neural network architecture designed to model long-range temporal dependencies, superseding standard RNNs in dialogue modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) is a category of recurrent neural network architecture designed to process sequential data and capture long-range word order dependencies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b6673cfdbb7f8a448709da4e46192b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bob">
      <data key="d0">Bob</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Bob is an English given name cited as the canonical base form in an example illustrating hypocoristic modification.&lt;SEP&gt;Bob is an exemplary subject referenced in illustrative sentences to demonstrate word order dependencies in natural language.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-195b3bb495c9171fc33fb85c129c4366</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Marry">
      <data key="d0">Marry</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Marry is an exemplary object/subject referenced in illustrative sentences used to demonstrate how word order affects sentence semantics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Learning">
      <data key="d0">Deep Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A branch of machine learning utilizing multi-layered neural networks suited for complex representations and sequence processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of machine learning algorithms based on artificial neural networks that learn representations of data across multiple processing layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A subfield of machine learning based on artificial neural networks that learns hierarchical representations for various complex NLP tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A subfield of machine learning using deep neural network architectures that serves as a foundational technique for modern dialogue systems and conversational data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;An advanced subfield of machine learning identified as an upcoming technique for analyzing opinions and emotions in social media texts.&lt;SEP&gt;An advanced subset of machine learning models, including CNNs and RNNs, that catalyzed major breakthroughs in large-scale food database analysis and multi-modal feature fusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning encompasses advanced artificial neural network architectures recently applied to Twitter sentiment classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning is a category of machine learning methodologies utilizing neural architectures such as encoder-decoder models for natural language generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning is a class of machine learning algorithms based on artificial neural networks with multiple layers, used widely across natural language processing and ABSA tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning is a subfield of machine learning utilizing multi-layered neural networks to learn continuous vector representations of words and sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning refers to neural network-based approaches utilized in NLP tasks including sentiment analysis, opinion lexicon building, and subword modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning is a subfield of artificial intelligence utilizing multi-layer neural architectures for representation learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning is a subset of machine learning based on artificial neural networks that facilitates representation learning across complex NLP tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6482c4aa158143b58b33b61435191e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3194fa4581f2aaec823530e030775b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9314a3266fc8d0bc21af4b765fa25b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcb2d684d656e9d9c24124949d2aaf80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f148e57eed21f7948ba04d2d12e56d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f22646227380376cc403c82c1f4615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e060c5bbcfa40d71aa9fb0a2e63bff30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c672772b311a70f628b5b6b878eb3f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c233285dd27a358f6bf38c2050006d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f43d3218257ab88ccde621eadece2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feature Engineering">
      <data key="d0">Feature Engineering</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Feature Engineering is a traditional machine learning approach relying on hand-crafted features such as n-gram overlaps and dependency trees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Composition">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Composition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Semantic Composition is a category of linguistic and computational modeling focused on deriving the meaning of phrases and sentences from their constituent words.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Max-Pooling">
      <data key="d0">Max-Pooling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of feature aggregation operations in neural networks that extracts the most prominent features from representations.&lt;SEP&gt;Max-Pooling is a neural network pooling operation used to extract dominant global features across context windows but lacking sensitivity to word order.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Level Comparison">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Level Comparison</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A framework and methodological category for evaluating similarity and relations between sentences across word-word, sentence-sentence, and word-sentence levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-Level Comparison is a comparative framework evaluating textual relations simultaneously across word-word, sentence-sentence, and word-sentence levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-Level Comparison is an evaluation and representation framework applied to encoders that generate multi-aspect word and sentence embeddings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gradient Boosting">
      <data key="d0">Gradient Boosting</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Gradient Boosting is a machine learning ensemble technique utilized to combine heterogeneous features for sentence similarity prediction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XGBoost">
      <data key="d0">XGBoost</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">XGBoost is a gradient boosting regression algorithm whose parameters are configured and reported in the sentiment analysis experimental results.&lt;SEP&gt;XGBoost is an optimized gradient boosting library and algorithmic category implemented in competitive STS ensemble architectures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf3bb0dbc6eb81bded1d21569d42693f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e060c5bbcfa40d71aa9fb0a2e63bff30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Classification">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of natural language processing tasks focused on categorizing sentences or predicting relations and target labels between sentence pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentence Classification is an NLP task category where entire sentences are assigned predefined class labels, such as sentiment or topic classes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f43d3218257ab88ccde621eadece2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M-MaxLSTM-CNN Model">
      <data key="d0">M-MaxLSTM-CNN Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep neural network architecture that jointly applies CNN on multiple pre-trained word embeddings to learn multi-aspect embeddings, encodes sentences using max-pooling and LSTM, and measures sentence similarity via multi-level comparison.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MGNC-CNN">
      <data key="d0">MGNC-CNN</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline or comparative neural network model whose authors apply independent CNNs on each pre-trained word embedding for extracting features and then concatenate them for sentence classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cosine Similarity">
      <data key="d0">Cosine Similarity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical similarity metric used within the sentence-sentence comparison level to measure the directional alignment between two sentence embedding vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric and mathematical measure of similarity between two document vectors calculated from their dot product normalized by the product of their magnitudes.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric used to measure the cosine of the angle between two multidimensional vectors, utilized here to evaluate similarity between TF-IDF representations of texts.&lt;SEP&gt;A similarity metric computed between sense embeddings and context word embeddings to capture semantic compatibility in WSD tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A vector similarity metric used to rank word pairs based on the angle between their embedding representations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cosine similarity is a geometric distance metric used to evaluate semantic proximity between word vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Cosine similarity is a geometric metric measuring the cosine of the angle between two vectors, utilized to evaluate the similarity between sentence or summary vectors and the centroid vector.&lt;SEP&gt;Cosine similarity is a metric used to measure semantic closeness between vector representations of target senses and surrounding context words.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d061db4b0ef06b5f3c1d715a602dc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9539a4c4fcbd235bc0ccbc8f3fd26a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd39034576eb8de5d243305db77f4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626602288681ee562ad75771b687c6be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad8b9a3ff673a8919c974c24205949f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc72a8696f96f81ea7b13e31bd1a5bbb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Neural Difference">
      <data key="d0">Neural Difference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A parameterized neural metric that measures differences between sentence embeddings using weight matrices and bias parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multiplication Vector &amp; Absolute Difference">
      <data key="d0">Multiplication Vector &amp; Absolute Difference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A composite comparison metric employing element-wise multiplication and absolute subtraction between sentence embedding vectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A functional component and methodological stage in the model responsible for transforming sequences of word embeddings into unified sentence representations using max-pooling and LSTM.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Aspect Word Embedding">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Aspect Word Embedding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A rich distributed word representation learned by jointly applying convolutional filters across multiple pre-trained word embeddings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ab7a441df1622290b22727fa248712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Crawl">
      <data key="d0">Common Crawl</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A non-profit organization that maintains an open repository of web crawl data, which was used to pre-train the GloVe word embeddings.&lt;SEP&gt;A non-profit organization that provides open web crawl data, whose 840-billion-token corpus was used to train the GloVe word embedding model.&lt;SEP&gt;Common Crawl (referred to as CC) is an organization/project producing web-crawled text corpora, used to measure language representation against country populations.&lt;SEP&gt;Common Crawl is an open web data repository providing large-scale web-crawled text used to evaluate global linguistic representation and population densities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d721fe5dad0029252753a2c12969e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f52e20fe32ec91903501f1422f3fe621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06cb5cf31459df4733b688cf007ff6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Baroni">
      <data key="d0">Baroni</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher who developed a context-predict 400-dimensional semantic word embedding model trained on ukWaC, English Wikipedia, and the British National Corpus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pre-Trained Word Embeddings">
      <data key="d0">Pre-Trained Word Embeddings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of vector representations of words and phrases, including word2vec, fastText, GloVe, Baroni, and SL999, studied and combined for sentence modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Modeling Approaches">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Modeling Approaches</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of neural and compositional methods used to represent sentence semantics, including Word Average, Project Average, LSTM, Max-CNN, and M-MaxLSTM-CNN.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="British National Corpus">
      <data key="d0">British National Corpus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A curated text corpus of British English used alongside ukWaC and Wikipedia to train the Baroni semantic word embedding model.&lt;SEP&gt;The British National Corpus (BNC) is a large text corpus of British English utilized by IRST-Kernels for unsupervised term proximity analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ukWaC">
      <data key="d0">ukWaC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A large web-crawled corpus of English text used to train the Baroni context-predict semantic embedding model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SICK">
      <data key="d0">SICK</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark dataset used to evaluate semantic textual similarity and relatedness models, characterized by smaller vocabulary size due to absence of named entities and idioms.&lt;SEP&gt;SICK (Sentences Involving Compositional Knowledge) is an evaluation benchmark dataset containing textual relatedness (SICK-R) and textual entailment (SICK-E) tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STSB">
      <data key="d0">STSB</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">STSB (Semantic Textual Similarity Benchmark) is a dataset used to evaluate semantic textual similarity models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Semantic Textual Similarity Benchmark dataset containing complex sentence pairs, used for grid search hyper-parameter tuning and overall evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PPDB">
      <data key="d0">PPDB</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Paraphrase Database containing word pairs, used to train the SL999 word embedding model under a skip-gram objective with negative sampling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SimLex-999">
      <data key="d0">SimLex-999</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A semantic similarity dataset referenced as the tuning resource for the SL999 pre-trained word embedding model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Google News Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Google News Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A large text dataset containing 100 billion tokens developed by Google, used to train the 300-dimensional word2vec model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aa01d1737dbc0f2a321f7d1e6e0289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nguyen Tien Huy">
      <data key="d0">Nguyen Tien Huy</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Nguyen Tien Huy is a researcher who conducted the described work on sentence embeddings and multi-level comparison while serving as an intern at Toshiba Research Center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Toshiba Research Center">
      <data key="d0">Toshiba Research Center</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Toshiba Research Center is an industrial research facility where Nguyen Tien Huy worked as an intern to conduct this research.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M-MaxLSTM-CNN">
      <data key="d0">M-MaxLSTM-CNN</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">M-MaxLSTM-CNN is a neural network model architecture that combines MaxLSTM-CNN encoders and multi-level comparison across multiple pre-trained word embeddings to measure semantic textual relationships.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="InferSent">
      <data key="d0">InferSent</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">InferSent is a neural sentence embedding model that uses transfer knowledge learned on textual entailment data.&lt;SEP&gt;InferSent is a sentence similarity model architecture fine-tuned via transfer learning to measure semantic similarity between activity phrases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22507f0961c9cfd8c5355551b99d5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HCTI">
      <data key="d0">HCTI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">HCTI is a neural sentence representation model serving as a benchmark on the STSB dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MRPC">
      <data key="d0">MRPC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">MRPC (Microsoft Research Paraphrase Corpus) is an evaluation dataset used to assess textual similarity and paraphrase identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LibriVoxDe">
      <data key="d0">LibriVoxDe</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">LibriVoxDe is an organization or project referenced in the document.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SL999">
      <data key="d0">SL999</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SL999 is a pre-trained word embedding trained on the paraphrase database, evaluated for its vocabulary coverage and performance on textual similarity tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Max-CNN">
      <data key="d0">Max-CNN</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Max-CNN is a neural sentence encoder model that generates sentence embeddings using convolutional neural networks and pooling, evaluated in comparison with MaxLSTM-CNN.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MaxLSTM-CNN">
      <data key="d0">MaxLSTM-CNN</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">MaxLSTM-CNN is a neural encoder combining Long Short-Term Memory networks and convolutional neural networks to capture word order and generate multi-aspect representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Word Average">
      <data key="d0">Word Average</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Word Average is a simple compositional architecture that averages word vectors to represent sentences, used as a baseline for STS tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Project Average">
      <data key="d0">Project Average</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Average is a parameterized compositional model for learning sentence embeddings from word embeddings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LSTM">
      <data key="d0">LSTM</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of recurrent neural network architecture featuring gated mechanisms, used as encoders and decoders in the imaginator modules.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture used as a foundation for generating agent and user utterances in the imaginator component.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network architecture used to encode extracted segments from previous SQL queries in the segment copying procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurrent neural network variant suited for sequence modeling, serving as encoder and decoder networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture designed to model temporal and sequential patterns in data.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture used in forward and backward configurations to read subword character sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture used to capture non-local and non-linear dependencies across character sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture used to capture word order and global relationships across sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network architecture, used in 2-layer bidirectional and unidirectional configurations within the encoder and decoder.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory networks are recurrent neural network architectures used to compute representations of mention chains and global features.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory networks, a type of recurrent neural network architecture used to encode context and generate personalized responses in dialogue systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory neural network architecture whose hidden state sizes and parameter capacities were tested against multilingual scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory recurrent neural network architecture utilized as an utterance generator attending to node embeddings in DynoNet.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory recurrent neural networks utilized in coreference resolution to construct mention-chain representations and global features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e97e9e342e051e03614c8dcaa59a2bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb3ab7fc50f538bef2c8ddb57a8a6b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f7cfb64157b0b1becf1f72e036758aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-275b54efb44b71f0c8102cd8da9ac971&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6907deaed642269724a32b0c9ccd9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3a4a211bb43ab387afa7488082157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb0afdde0d066987770f69fd6c4b0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a22c5897192a959774723efeba8a377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70218d643d3a2f540abe4bb2afd6986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dddef9c6531f0d5588d28af861e6bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17dc83295bc11d415f3f0d85e84a5a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15b5829d32b6817e2c4e142dba61455b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad4815afd1a11fd7bc1c72c7da255e9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebac0f3b43edbff22438f6ec756f16fb</data>
    </node>
