      <data key="d3">chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computational Linguistics">
      <data key="d0">Computational Linguistics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Computational Linguistics is an interdisciplinary field of study focusing on using computational models and natural language processing to analyze text, including obituary data.&lt;SEP&gt;Computational linguistics is a scientific discipline that explores language modeling, corpus normalization, and computational analysis of multilingual texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06cb5cf31459df4733b688cf007ff6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer is a group of diseases involving abnormal cell growth, for which real-time mortality surveillance was evaluated using French online obituaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Health Records">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Health Records</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of digitized clinical documentation storing patient health data, largely composed of natural language text utilized for decision making and policy formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital medical documentation (EHRs) containing unstructured clinical information from which entities and relationships are extracted.&lt;SEP&gt;Electronic Health Records (EHRs) is a category of digital patient health information and clinical documentation used to support medical care, clinical decision making, and healthcare policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Electronic health records are digital versions of patients' paper charts used in linkage studies with online obituary notices to track mortality data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1fb2eeb8c8333a70050efefb9412104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f5016d3aa81277cabc5c947f1ca64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Narrative Schemas">
      <data key="d0">Narrative Schemas</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Narrative schemas are structured representations of event sequences and relationships within texts analyzed across document categories including obituaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gender Bias">
      <data key="d0">Gender Bias</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A form of social bias evaluated within artificial intelligence and natural language processing systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic disparity in dataset representation or model prediction accuracy across gender categories in relation extraction and NLP tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic disparity in prediction performance or representation reflecting demographic gender differences in machine learning models and datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;Gender bias is a form of social bias characterized by systematic disparities in model performance and representation when processing data related to different genders.&lt;SEP&gt;Gender bias represents systematic disparities in the depiction of men and women, such as differences in personal life versus professional focus found in obituaries and biographies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bac16ae7b48f68b81dcf01699b27c93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31134945186e62e7effccb3ba89b180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1405d1609fdbebb00fe9dd18235f8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c233285dd27a358f6bf38c2050006d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-362346ad5b3a18dced3a68b0e282ea62</data>
    </node>
