    <node id="US">
      <data key="d0">US</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The US (United States) is a country identified as having over-predicted languages on Twitter compared to census data.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is identified as being over-represented in Twitter data relative to its population size.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is one of the countries from which crowd workers were accepted for annotation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country whose regular citizens and social media users were mimicked and targeted by IRA troll campaigns during political events.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States, a geographic region from which AMT crowd workers were selected to annotate relation statements.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States, one of the geographical sources for the annotated obituary dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States, referenced in the context of IRA trolls mimicking the slang and language of US citizens.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States, where the confidential doctor-patient relationship and medical data are legally protected under federal privacy rules.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef7b95a2f35faad97942f87543b7ab1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f30e651d33c86668592dd08985152d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7d53ab63937232bbcc4be9c7080dd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd3cd3db55d1536871b82317efd46a4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d721fe5dad0029252753a2c12969e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56672a5cb0c14c3d38c148dbe5205622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-362346ad5b3a18dced3a68b0e282ea62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9645cad08b5b060013cac117d156f888</data>
