    <node id="Ukuxhumana">
      <data key="d0">Ukuxhumana</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An open-source research project and GitHub repository hosting machine translation code and datasets for South African languages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f50b15c876beec2eae8bf6437e8409aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Meta-Learning">
      <data key="d0">Meta-Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An advanced machine learning methodology proposed for future research to tackle low-resourced African language translation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f50b15c876beec2eae8bf6437e8409aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Zero-Shot Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Zero-Shot Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine translation methods requiring no direct parallel training data, identified as potential future work to cover all official South African languages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f50b15c876beec2eae8bf6437e8409aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concept-to-Text Generation">
      <data key="d0">Concept-to-Text Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specialized branch of natural language generation that transforms structured knowledge representations, such as ontologies, into fluent text.&lt;SEP&gt;Concept-to-text generation is a specialized natural language generation task that converts structured ontological data or conceptual representations into coherent multi-sentence text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Integer Linear Programming">
      <data key="d0">Integer Linear Programming</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical optimization framework (ILP) used in the extended model to globally optimize sentence planning, aggregation, and natural language generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical optimization framework used to jointly model content selection, lexicalization, and sentence aggregation for producing compact texts.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical optimization framework utilized to jointly optimize content selection, lexicalization, and sentence aggregation in text generation to produce compact texts.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical optimization technique (ILP) widely applied in natural language processing and generation tasks to jointly optimize decisions such as content selection, aggregation, ordering, and lexicalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer Linear Programming (ILP) is a mathematical optimization approach applied to jointly solve content selection, lexicalization, and sentence aggregation in natural language generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer Linear Programming (ILP) is a mathematical optimization framework used in this context to model fact selection and sentence aggregation under specific objective functions and constraints.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pipeline architecture is a traditional software and NLG architectural paradigm where components execute sequentially in separate, greedy stages.&lt;SEP&gt;A traditional multi-stage system architecture for natural language generation that executes content selection, text planning, lexicalization, and realization sequentially.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Linked Data">
      <data key="d0">Linked Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A paradigm for publishing structured, interconnected data on the Web using Semantic Web standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Linked Data refers to a method of publishing structured data using semantic web technologies, RDF triples, and SPARQL queries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb73055a3a263fcef16382513853f022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Description Logics">
      <data key="d0">Description Logics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A family of formal knowledge representation formalisms that provide the logical foundation for Semantic Web ontology languages like OWL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RDF Schema">
      <data key="d0">RDF Schema</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A semantic extension of RDF providing mechanisms for describing groups of related resources and classes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content Selection">
      <data key="d0">Content Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A stage in natural language generation pipelines that chooses the logical facts or axioms from an ontology to be expressed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in natural language generation that determines which available facts from a knowledge source are selected to be communicated.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in natural language generation that determines which facts from an ontology or data source should be conveyed in the output text.&lt;SEP&gt;A subtask in natural language generation focused on choosing which facts to express, computationally analogous to the multiple knapsack problem.&lt;SEP&gt;A subtask in natural language generation that determines which facts or information from a knowledge pool or database should be expressed in the output text.&lt;SEP&gt;Content selection is a sub-task and process in natural language generation systems that determines which facts from an ontology are chosen for inclusion in generated texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Content selection is a subtask in natural language generation that determines which information units or facts from the input data should be expressed in the output text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Text Planning">
      <data key="d0">Text Planning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A stage in natural language generation that determines the sequence of facts, sentence order, and rhetorical structure of a text.&lt;SEP&gt;An overarching natural language generation stage that governs the discourse structure, organization, and ordering of generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lexicalization">
      <data key="d0">Lexicalization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language generation stage that selects vocabulary, phrasing, and sentence plans to express facts in linguistic form.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in natural language generation responsible for choosing the vocabulary, words, and syntactic structures used to express selected facts.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in natural language generation that selects the specific words and syntactic structures used to express individual facts.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in text generation involving the selection of appropriate words and syntactic phrases to express chosen concepts or facts.&lt;SEP&gt;Lexicalization is a subtask in natural language generation responsible for choosing specific words and syntactic forms to express concepts and relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Aggregation">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Aggregation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language generation process that merges multiple facts or clauses into single sentences to improve text flow, compactness, and readability.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language generation process that merges multiple simple sentences or sentence plans into concise, aggregated sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language processing technique that combines multiple simple sentences or semantic facts into complex, cohesive sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A process in natural language generation that combines multiple facts or simple clauses into unified, cohesive, and compact sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;An NLG process that merges multiple shorter sentences into fewer, longer sentences to improve compactness and readability.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentence aggregation is a natural language generation process that combines multiple facts into compact subsets to produce coherent, aggregated sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentence aggregation is an NLG subtask that combines multiple simple semantic messages or sentences into single, more complex sentences to reduce redundancy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Referring Expression Generation">
      <data key="d0">Referring Expression Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A component of NLG that generates appropriate referring forms, such as pronouns or noun phrases, to identify entities in discourse.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language generation subtask focused on producing appropriate noun phrases or pronouns to identify referents unambiguously in discourse.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language generation subtask focused on selecting the most appropriate names, nouns, or descriptions for entities and classes.&lt;SEP&gt;Referring expression generation is an NLG subtask that selects appropriate linguistic expressions to identify domain entities in text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Surface Realization">
      <data key="d0">Surface Realization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The final natural language generation phase that converts structured linguistic representations into grammatically correct surface text.&lt;SEP&gt;The final stage in natural language generation that transforms abstract linguistic structures into actual strings of words according to syntactic and morphological rules.&lt;SEP&gt;The final stage of natural language generation that converts abstract internal linguistic representations into actual textual strings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Over-Generate and Rank">
      <data key="d0">Over-Generate and Rank</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An architectural strategy in NLG that produces multiple alternative candidates at each stage and ranks them to mitigate greedy pipeline decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa0a1d40aed971d10ad0f0f2c4938cf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="StEmilionRegion">
      <data key="d0">StEmilionRegion</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A geographic region referenced in the ontology as the location where StEmilion wine is produced.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949</data>
    </node>
    <node id="StEmilion">
      <data key="d0">StEmilion</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A class in the wine ontology defined as an intersection of Bordeaux wines, located in the St. Emilion region, possessing strong flavor, red color, and made from Cabernet Sauvignon grapes.&lt;SEP&gt;StEmilion (Saint-Émilion) is a renowned wine-producing region and appellation in southwestern France, featured as an individual entity in the ontology and sentence planning examples.&lt;SEP&gt;StEmilion refers to Saint-Émilion, a prominent wine-producing region used as an example subject in the sentence plan templates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
