      <data key="d3">chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Naturalowl">
      <data key="d0">Naturalowl</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language generation system whose text planner and referring expression generation components are utilized by the experimental systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An open-source natural language generation system for OWL ontologies that implements typical NLG processing stages and serves as the baseline and integration platform for the ILP models.&lt;SEP&gt;NaturalOWL is an ontology-based natural language generation system that utilizes a pipeline architecture and domain-dependent linguistic resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Naturalowl is an open-source, publicly available natural language generation system designed for OWL ontologies that originally operated using a pipeline architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cabernet Sauvignon">
      <data key="d0">Cabernet Sauvignon</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A grape variety defined as an ingredient property value for the StEmilion wine class within the OWL wine ontology.&lt;SEP&gt;Cabernet Sauvignon is a grape variety and wine category used in the linguistic aggregation and text generation examples.&lt;SEP&gt;Cabernet Sauvignon is a grape variety identified in the ontology as the exclusive grape used to make St. Emilion wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcb14d19cf40f8290f78e99be61a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
