    </node>
    <node id="Message Triple">
      <data key="d0">Message Triple</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A formal semantic representation of a fact consisting of a target individual or class, a relation, and an object, serving as the input for text generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A message triple is a semantic representation category comprising a subject, relation, and object used by NaturalOWL to prepare ontology facts for verbalization.&lt;SEP&gt;A semantic data unit composed of a subject, property/relation, and object used as input for natural language generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured semantic representation consisting of subject, predicate, and object elements (such as facts) used as input for text generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RDF Triple">
      <data key="d0">RDF Triple</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An RDF triple is a standard Semantic Web statement category from which message triples are adapted with potential relation modifiers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Plan">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A sentence plan is a linguistic template category in NaturalOWL that dictates how a specific relation within a message triple is expressed in natural language.&lt;SEP&gt;A sentence plan is an intermediate linguistic structure used to verbalize facts, composed of distinct elements that contribute to the length and structure of aggregated sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured linguistic plan consisting of distinct elements and referring expressions designed to produce natural language sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured linguistic template comprising slots and instructions that define how to verbalize a semantic fact or message triple into a natural language sentence.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured sequence of annotated linguistic slots used in natural language generation to realize semantic relations into natural text.&lt;SEP&gt;Sentence Plan is a structural template category in NaturalOWL that defines how to construct sentences expressing ontological message triples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2133007f11cdae6d7728268eadeba6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Language Name">
      <data key="d0">Natural Language Name</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A linguistic expression or designation (nl name) used to indirectly express facts or reference concepts within generated text.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language name (nl name) is a structured category consisting of annotated slots used to generate noun phrases for ontology classes and individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Language Name (NL Name) is a structured linguistic specification category in NaturalOWL composed of annotated slots that describe an individual or class.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2133007f11cdae6d7728268eadeba6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ontology Verbalizer">
      <data key="d0">Ontology Verbalizer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An ontology verbalizer is a category of natural language generation tools that translate formal OWL ontologies into human-readable text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="User Model">
      <data key="d0">User Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A user model is a computational profiling category utilized by NaturalOWL to select and prioritize the most important message triples for generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-931b1517ef4e7994e14d3ac80d1af80b</data>
    </node>
