    </node>
    <node id="Wine">
      <data key="d0">Wine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A broad category of alcoholic beverage produced from fermented grapes, serving as the parent classification for Chardonnay, Bancroft Chardonnay, and St. Emilion.&lt;SEP&gt;A category of alcoholic beverage made from fermented grapes, used as an ontological concept in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A category representing wines, wine producers, wineries, and regions modeled in the Wine Ontology for text generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain category of beverages, encompassing types such as Sauternes and Riesling, used as the subject matter for the initial natural language generation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is a broad beverage and product category utilized as a head noun concept in ontology triples and linguistic phrasing examples.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is a general category of beverage that serves as a superclass in the ontology message triples described in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2133007f11cdae6d7728268eadeba6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
