    </node>
    <node id="Cabernet Sauvignon Grape">
      <data key="d0">Cabernet Sauvignon Grape</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A grape variety used in wine production, cited as an example object in natural language generation sentence planning.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific variety of red wine grape used as an ingredient in winemaking, specifically for St. Emilion.&lt;SEP&gt;Cabernet Sauvignon Grape is a category of wine grape variety referenced in semantic relation triples for wine composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Cabernet Sauvignon Grape is a grape category and raw ingredient referenced in the sentence generation plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NaturalOWL">
      <data key="d0">NaturalOWL</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An open-source natural language generation system and research project designed to generate coherent natural language descriptions from OWL ontologies.&lt;SEP&gt;NaturalOWL is an ontology-to-text natural language generation system and research project whose aggregation rules and sentence plans are used for verbalizing semantic knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;NaturalOWL is an open-source natural language generation engine and research project that generates descriptions from OWL ontologies using sentence planning, aggregation rules, and importance scores.&lt;SEP&gt;NaturalOWL is an open-source natural language generation system and engine designed to produce fluent descriptions from OWL ontologies and semantic triples.&lt;SEP&gt;NaturalOWL is an open-source natural language generation system and framework designed to produce descriptions of semantic web ontology individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Red">
      <data key="d0">Red</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A color attribute and category used to describe wine, specifically referenced in relation to St. Emilion.&lt;SEP&gt;Red is a color category and ontological attribute associated with Red Wine in the semantic triple :hasColor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Strong">
      <data key="d0">Strong</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A flavor characteristic and descriptive category applied to wine within ontological triples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f9304f4481df329096caee5332f6d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="White Bordeaux">
      <data key="d0">White Bordeaux</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">White Bordeaux is a category of white wine originating from the Bordeaux region, cited to illustrate redundant relations in natural language generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Product">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Product</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electronic Product is a product category used as an example domain for topical section partitioning based on attributes like size, weight, material, and features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Demonstrative Noun Phrase">
      <data key="d0">Demonstrative Noun Phrase</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Demonstrative Noun Phrase is a linguistic category of referring expression (such as 'this wine') generated to avoid repetitive naming.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5dc202cbcb7ba0bcd01a26bba74ac644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mountadam">
      <data key="d0">Mountadam</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Mountadam is a wine producer referenced as the maker of wines such as Bancroft Chardonnay and Mountadam Riesling.&lt;SEP&gt;Mountadam is a winery and producer mentioned as the maker of Bancroft Chardonnay in the natural language generation examples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bancroft">
      <data key="d0">Bancroft</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A winery or wine producer that manufactures Bancroft Chardonnay.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft is a geographical location identified as the place where Bancroft Chardonnay is produced.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft is a geographical location where Bancroft Chardonnay is made.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft is a wine maker or producer responsible for making Bancroft Chardonnay.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft is a wine producer or maker referenced in the ontology and natural language generation examples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bancroft Chardonnay">
      <data key="d0">Bancroft Chardonnay</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific wine category and product produced by Bancroft in the Napa Region, used as an ontology subject in natural language generation examples.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft Chardonnay is a specific category and variety of wine used as an example entity in the sentence planning and aggregation models.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft Chardonnay is a specific wine product characterized as a moderate flavor, dry Chardonnay produced in the Napa Region by Bancroft.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft Chardonnay is a specific wine product or class used as an example entity in the ILP natural language generation model.&lt;SEP&gt;Bancroft Chardonnay is a wine variety and product produced by Mountadam and made in Bancroft, used as an example in sentence planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILP Model">
      <data key="d0">ILP Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Integer Linear Programming formulation used to predict sentence length and jointly optimize content selection, lexicalization, and sentence aggregation.&lt;SEP&gt;An Integer Linear Programming model applied in natural language generation to optimize sentence aggregation and prevent unnatural sentence combinations across topical sections.&lt;SEP&gt;The integer linear programming formulation whose variable count grows exponentially with the number of fact subsets and available facts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Text Planner">
      <data key="d0">Text Planner</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language generation component from Naturalowl that partitions facts into topical sections and orders sections, facts, and sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural language generation module responsible for ordering simple sentences, topical sections, and aggregated sentences within the discourse generation pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;The Text Planner is an architectural component in NaturalOWL and Pipeline responsible for partitioning selected facts into topical sections and ordering them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Aggregation Rules">
      <data key="d0">Aggregation Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Aggregation rules are linguistic resources shared across the generation systems to combine and structure multiple facts within topical sections into coherent sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;Syntactic and semantic rules provided by NaturalOWL that merge multiple ordered simple sentences into concise, fluent aggregated sentences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282fad0c34bc4ff28878e675e843b8a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mountadam Riesling">
      <data key="d0">Mountadam Riesling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mountadam Riesling is a wine individual and product in the ontology, characterized as a medium, dry, delicate Riesling produced by Mountadam.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Riesling">
      <data key="d0">Riesling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Riesling is a white wine category described in the generation texts as having sweet taste and full body.&lt;SEP&gt;Riesling is a wine category and grape variety to which Mountadam Riesling belongs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OWL Ontology">
      <data key="d0">OWL Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A knowledge representation framework used to define individuals, classes, and facts, providing the structured input data for natural language generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-796a1e011fcb40990be73e06c4bc0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fact Selection">
      <data key="d0">Fact Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A stage in natural language generation modeled by integer linear programming where specific communicative facts are chosen for inclusion based on their importance and length trade-offs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objective Function">
      <data key="d0">Objective Function</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical formulation designed to maximize the priority of expressing important facts while minimizing the length of distinct elements and natural language names in generated text.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical formulation in the integer linear programming model that maximizes fact importance while minimizing sentence plan elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importance Scores">
      <data key="d0">Importance Scores</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Numerical values assigned to facts to quantify their significance, used by the model to prioritize fact selection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Message Triples">
      <data key="d0">Message Triples</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Semantic representations of facts that are evaluated for inclusion, which may be assigned zero importance scores if redundant.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Topical Sections">
      <data key="d0">Topical Sections</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Thematic partitions of facts used to enforce aggregation constraints, ensuring facts from different topics are not combined unnaturally.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89649e5a10f10d3f6abdf11541607a36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disease Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Disease Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A biomedical domain ontology characterized by facts with conjuncts and varied natural language naming lengths.&lt;SEP&gt;A biomedical domain ontology characterized by varied natural language name lengths and conjunctions, used to evaluate extended ILP and baseline text generation models.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease Ontology is a formal biomedical ontology used as an experimental dataset for evaluating concept-to-text natural language generation systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disease Ontology is a biomedical domain ontology comprising development classes used in the third set of natural language generation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disease Ontology is a biomedical knowledge base and ontology resource used in experiments to provide structured medical facts and vocabulary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disease Ontology is a domain ontology representing diseases, referenced as a point of comparison in text generation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disease Ontology is a formal ontology describing diseases, containing 6,746 classes, 15 relations, and 1,545 individuals, used as the knowledge base for NLG experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disease Ontology is a structured biomedical knowledge domain used as a dataset for evaluating natural language generation systems and sentence aggregation models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Brazilian Hemorrhagic Fever">
      <data key="d0">Brazilian Hemorrhagic Fever</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Brazilian Hemorrhagic Fever is a viral infectious disease caused by the Sabia virus and transmitted by rodents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Viral Infectious Disease">
      <data key="d0">Viral Infectious Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical classification (DOID_934) under which diseases caused by viral infections, such as Rift Valley Fever, are categorized.&lt;SEP&gt;Viral Infectious Disease is a broad category of illnesses caused by pathogenic viruses, encompassing conditions like Brazilian hemorrhagic fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sabia Virus">
      <data key="d0">Sabia Virus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sabia virus is an infectious viral agent identified as the material basis and causative agent of Brazilian hemorrhagic fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Napa Region">
      <data key="d0">Napa Region</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A prominent wine-producing geographic region where Bancroft Chardonnay is produced.&lt;SEP&gt;The Napa Region is a prominent wine-producing geographical area referenced as the origin of wines in the example sentences.&lt;SEP&gt;The Napa Region is a recognized geographical wine-producing region associated with the origin of certain wines such as Bancroft Chardonnay.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dfd4e1f2af27018cbd2ff675e9601171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chardonnay">
      <data key="d0">Chardonnay</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category and variety of white wine, representing the parent class of Bancroft Chardonnay.&lt;SEP&gt;Chardonnay is a category and varietal of white wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rodents">
      <data key="d0">Rodents</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rodents is a category of mammals identified as the transmission vector for Brazilian hemorrhagic fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Muscle Aches">
      <data key="d0">Muscle Aches</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Muscle aches is a medical symptom involving pain or soreness in muscles, documented as a symptom of Brazilian hemorrhagic fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dizziness">
      <data key="d0">Dizziness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Dizziness is an impairment in spatial perception and stability, categorized as a symptom of Brazilian hemorrhagic fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inflammation">
      <data key="d0">Inflammation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Inflammation is a medical condition and pathological process cited as an individual entity in the Disease Ontology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paralysis Of The Legs Due To Thrombosis Of Spinal Arteries">
      <data key="d0">Paralysis Of The Legs Due To Thrombosis Of Spinal Arteries</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paralysis of the legs due to thrombosis of spinal arteries is a specific medical condition used as an individual example within the Disease Ontology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03b4c3c4be893da83397ffc6784fbfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dry Wine">
      <data key="d0">Dry Wine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification category for wine sweetness denoting little to no residual sugar, exemplified by the :Dry property attribute.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Moderate Flavor">
      <data key="d0">Moderate Flavor</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A sensory categorization describing moderate flavor intensity within wine ontology specifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1636f27f377b367415be0a5806e2aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Constraints">
      <data key="d0">Constraints</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A set of mathematical restrictions (such as Eq. 34 and Eq. 35) limiting the word count of subsets and regulating the selection of sentences and natural language names for expressed facts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computational Complexity and Approximation">
      <data key="d0">Computational Complexity and Approximation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A theoretical category and section topic addressing the computational difficulty and approximation techniques associated with solving the optimization model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fact Expression">
      <data key="d0">Fact Expression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The selection and inclusion of informational facts ($f_i$) in the output text based on their relative importance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Generation">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The mechanism of generating explicit sentences ($a_i = 1$) for selected facts when they are not expressed via natural language names.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Word Limit Constraint">
      <data key="d0">Word Limit Constraint</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A constraint bounding the maximum number of words ($W_{max}$) allowed within each subset of generated text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Priority Weighting">
      <data key="d0">Priority Weighting</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tuning parameters ($\lambda_1, \lambda_2$) balancing the trade-off between maximizing expressed important facts and minimizing text length.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a12c0c800f66f36ecdd6e9a143afe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binary ILP Problems">
      <data key="d0">Binary ILP Problems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of mathematical optimization problems where all variables are restricted to binary values, known in general to be NP-hard.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP-Hard">
      <data key="d0">NP-Hard</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A complexity class of computational problems that are at least as difficult as the hardest problems in NP, including binary ILP and knapsack problems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0-1 Multiple Knapsack Problem">
      <data key="d0">0-1 Multiple Knapsack Problem</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A combinatorial optimization problem class where items are packed into multiple knapsacks of given capacities, closely related to content selection in text generation models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Linear Programming">
      <data key="d0">Linear Programming</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical optimization framework with continuous variables used in LP relaxation to approximate integer linear programming solutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Electronics Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Electronics Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A domain ontology containing product specifications with a large number of available facts per product, used to evaluate system scalability and approximation methods.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain ontology covering electronic products, characterized by unique product names that limit alternative natural language naming.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain ontology utilized in the text generation experiments that required setting the subset parameter m to 5 or greater.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain-specific knowledge ontology utilized to provide concepts, text plans, and sentence plans for generating longer texts in the second experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain-specific ontology used in natural language generation experiments, containing an average of 14 facts and up to 21 facts per individual.&lt;SEP&gt;Consumer Electronics Ontology is a domain ontology containing knowledge about consumer electronic products, used to test solver efficiency and generation quality in NLG models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumer Electronics Ontology is a domain ontology covering product attributes and specifications, used to evaluate text conciseness and clarity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumer Electronics Ontology is a domain ontology previously used to evaluate natural language generation solver times and text aggregation models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumer Electronics Ontology is a domain ontology representing electronic products, discussed in relation to naming constraints in text generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="First ILP Model">
      <data key="d0">First ILP Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An integer linear programming model developed for text generation and content selection that operates effectively when the number of fact subsets is small (m &lt;= 4).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extended ILP Model">
      <data key="d0">Extended ILP Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An expanded integer linear programming formulation for text generation that accounts for natural language name variations and whose complexity grows exponentially with the number of fact subsets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Simplex Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">Simplex Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A widely used optimization algorithm for solving linear programming models, specifically utilized in solving linear programming relaxations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LP Relaxation">
      <data key="d0">LP Relaxation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An approximation technique in mathematical optimization where integer constraints are relaxed to continuous values to solve ILP problems in polynomial time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Totally Unimodular Matrix">
      <data key="d0">Totally Unimodular Matrix</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A matrix property where every square nonsingular submatrix has determinant 0, 1, or -1, guaranteeing integer solutions to linear programming relaxations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline Approach">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A conventional multistep architecture for natural language generation against which the ILP models and approximation methods are benchmarked.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Off-The-Shelf Solvers">
      <data key="d0">Off-The-Shelf Solvers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standard commercial or open-source mathematical programming solvers used to solve the original binary ILP models directly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ontology Evaluation Experiments">
      <data key="d0">Ontology Evaluation Experiments</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A series of experiments conducted to evaluate integer linear programming (ILP) models across multiple OWL ontologies representing different domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disease">
      <data key="d0">Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A broad biomedical domain category comprising thousands of disease classifications, their symptoms, and causes.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical entity category targeted for extraction in clinical named entity recognition tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Cameras">
      <data key="d0">Digital Cameras</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific product category within consumer electronics examined in the ontology text generation experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Camcorders">
      <data key="d0">Camcorders</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A consumer electronics product category used to test generation resources and ILP models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Printers">
      <data key="d0">Printers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A hardware and consumer electronics product category represented in the dataset and ontology evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rift Valley Fever">
      <data key="d0">Rift Valley Fever</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A viral infectious disease class (DOID_1328) that causes infection and various severe hemorrhagic symptoms in animals and humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Rift Valley Fever is a specific disease entity within the Disease Ontology mentioned in the context of definition strings and relation statements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rift Valley Fever Virus">
      <data key="d0">Rift Valley Fever Virus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The viral pathogen that forms the material basis of the Rift Valley Fever infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Aedes Mosquitoes">
      <data key="d0">Aedes Mosquitoes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The biological vector category responsible for transmitting the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Domestic Animals">
      <data key="d0">Domestic Animals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification of animals, including cattle, buffalo, sheep, goats, and camels, affected by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rift Valley">
      <data key="d0">Rift Valley</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A geographic region in Africa after which the Rift Valley fever and its associated virus are named.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Jaundice">
      <data key="d0">Jaundice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical symptom characterized by yellowing of the skin and eyes, identified as a symptom of Rift Valley Fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vomiting Blood">
      <data key="d0">Vomiting Blood</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A severe medical symptom involving hematemesis, listed as a clinical symptom resulting from Rift Valley Fever infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Passing Blood In The Feces">
      <data key="d0">Passing Blood In The Feces</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical symptom indicating internal gastrointestinal bleeding associated with Rift Valley Fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ecchymoses">
      <data key="d0">Ecchymoses</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A symptom caused by bleeding beneath the skin, manifesting as large bruises, associated with Rift Valley Fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bleeding From The Nose Or Gums">
      <data key="d0">Bleeding From The Nose Or Gums</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A hemorrhagic symptom involving mucocutaneous bleeding caused by Rift Valley Fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Menorrhagia">
      <data key="d0">Menorrhagia</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An abnormally heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding symptom associated with Rift Valley Fever infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bleeding From Venepuncture Sites">
      <data key="d0">Bleeding From Venepuncture Sites</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A clinical symptom characterized by persistent bleeding at needle insertion points, resulting from Rift Valley Fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Humans">
      <data key="d0">Humans</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A species and host category affected by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cattle">
      <data key="d0">Cattle</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of domestic livestock affected by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Buffalo">
      <data key="d0">Buffalo</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of domestic animal susceptible to infection by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sheep">
      <data key="d0">Sheep</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A domestic animal species vulnerable to infection and symptoms caused by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Goats">
      <data key="d0">Goats</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A domestic animal species affected by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Camels">
      <data key="d0">Camels</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A domestic animal category affected by the Rift Valley fever virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wine Producers">
      <data key="d0">Wine Producers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category representing individuals or entities engaged in the production of wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wineries">
      <data key="d0">Wineries</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of establishments and regions involved in wine making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manufacturers">
      <data key="d0">Manufacturers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Entities and companies that produce consumer electronics products such as printers and cameras.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biomedical Experts">
      <data key="d0">Biomedical Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Specialists in biomedical science who constructed the Disease Ontology to address real-life medical information needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="E-Commerce Experts">
      <data key="d0">E-Commerce Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Domain specialists who created the Consumer Electronics Ontology to address real-world electronic product information exchange.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac8f9f2211b931d8b94687fe3d4c425f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Evaggelakaki">
      <data key="d0">Evaggelakaki</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Evaggelakaki is a researcher cited for authoring domain-dependent generation resources and sentence planning benchmarks used in the Disease Ontology experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaggelakaki is a researcher whose 2014 experiments provided benchmark parameters for sentence aggregation and maximum sentence length used in natural language generation evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaggelakaki is a researcher whose 2014 work provided 200 randomly selected development classes and manually authored domain-dependent generation resources for NaturalOWL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language generation pipeline system used as a baseline for generating texts from ontology facts.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard pipeline baseline system that selects randomly among alternative natural language names to generate natural language text.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipeline is a conventional multi-stage baseline natural language generation system architecture evaluated against ILP models.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipeline is a standard pipeline-based natural language generation baseline system against which ilpnlgextend is benchmarked.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipeline is the experimental baseline model representing the original NaturalOWL architecture, using importance ranking and text planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ilpnlg">
      <data key="d0">Ilpnlg</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation system that jointly performs content selection, aggregation, and sentence planning assuming a single natural language name per entity.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilpnlg is a modified natural language generation model based on Integer Linear Programming that replaces the traditional pipeline architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilpnlg is an earlier Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation system referenced as a baseline comparison for ilpnlgextend.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ilpnlgextend">
      <data key="d0">Ilpnlgextend</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An extended Integer Linear Programming natural language generation system capable of handling multiple alternative natural language names and conjunctions.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilpnlgextend is an Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation system evaluated for handling varying name lengths, conjunctions, and multiple alternative natural language names.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilpnlgextend is an extended version of the Integer Linear Programming natural language generation model used in the experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipelinestoch">
      <data key="d0">Pipelinestoch</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A stochastic pipeline baseline system evaluated for text generation performance alongside other pipeline architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipelinestoch is a stochastic variant of the pipeline baseline that selects facts, sentence plans, and natural language names based on length-derived probabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipelineshort">
      <data key="d0">Pipelineshort</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pipeline baseline system that consistently selects the shortest available natural language name per individual and class.&lt;SEP&gt;A pipeline natural language generation variant that achieves slightly better fact-per-word ratios than the standard pipeline system.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipelineshort is a greedy variant of the pipeline baseline that prioritizes the shortest sentence plans and natural language names.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipelinebeam">
      <data key="d0">Pipelinebeam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pipeline baseline system using beam search that generates a fixed number of texts used as a benchmark for comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipelinebeam is a baseline NLG system that extends pipelineshort by employing beam search to select facts, sentence plans, names, and subsets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILP Models">
      <data key="d0">ILP Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of optimization-based natural language generation systems using Integer Linear Programming, including ilpnlg, ilpnlgextend, and ilpnlgapprox, designed to optimize content selection, aggregation, and referring expression generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer Linear Programming (ILP) models are optimization-based frameworks utilized by ilpnlg and ilpnlgextend as an alternative to traditional NLG pipeline architectures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded262becf3ee747d4ac144ff92895ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline Baselines">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline Baselines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of natural language generation baseline systems, including pipeline, pipelinestoch, pipelineshort, pipelinebeam, and pipelineshort*, that use standard pipeline architectures and varying selection strategies to generate texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wine Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Wine Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark ontology referenced for comparison, characterized by having fewer facts per individual (average of 5 facts) than the Consumer Electronics Ontology.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain ontology containing individuals and classes related to wines, used as a benchmark resource for text generation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain ontology used in natural language generation experiments to evaluate text compactness and the facts-per-words ratio produced by different systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wine Ontology is a conceptual domain ontology used to evaluate and compare the performance of integer linear programming and pipeline natural language generation systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wine Ontology is a structured conceptual knowledge domain used as a benchmark for testing natural language generation systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wine Ontology is a structured semantic knowledge base containing wine individuals and classes, used to evaluate natural language generation systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine Ontology is a domain-specific ontology representing wine knowledge, utilized as an experimental benchmark in natural language generation research.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wine Ontology Experiment">
      <data key="d0">Wine Ontology Experiment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation comparing ilpnlg to baseline pipeline systems on the Wine Ontology, demonstrating higher compactness without loss of perceived quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Electronics Ontology Experiment">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Electronics Ontology Experiment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation assessing ilpnlg and its approximation ilpnlgapprox against baselines on product data requiring multi-bucket aggregation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disease Ontology Experiment">
      <data key="d0">Disease Ontology Experiment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation testing ilpnlg and ilpnlgextend against baseline pipelines to address variable name lengths and conjunctions in biomedical data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Referring Expression Generation Component">
      <data key="d0">Referring Expression Generation Component</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A component of the Naturalowl system responsible for replacing selected natural language names with demonstratives, demonstrative noun phrases, or pronouns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipelineshort*">
      <data key="d0">Pipelineshort*</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An advanced variant of pipelineshort that selects the shortest sentence plan and the natural language name that indirectly expresses the largest number of facts.&lt;SEP&gt;An enhanced or modified variant of the pipelineshort system benchmarked against ILPNLGExtend.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipelineshort* is a modified version of the pipeline NLG system tested alongside pipeline and ilpnlgextend.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ilpnlgapprox">
      <data key="d0">Ilpnlgapprox</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An approximation of the ilpnlg system designed for computational efficiency by generating each sentence of the text separately.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilpnlgapprox is a variant or approximation version of the ILP natural language generation system evaluated for facts-per-word efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0cb33fcc0fb3d5756d3d8c1ec3bc2eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wine Ontology Experiments">
      <data key="d0">Wine Ontology Experiments</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation designed to assess the performance, aggregation, and compactness of natural language generation systems using data from the Wine Ontology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disease Ontology Experiments">
      <data key="d0">Disease Ontology Experiments</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Experiments evaluating natural language generation performance on the Disease Ontology, which prompted the development of the extended ilpnlgextend system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Language Generation Systems">
      <data key="d0">Natural Language Generation Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of computational systems, including ilpnlg, ilpnlgextend, pipeline, and pipelineshort, used to generate English texts from ontological facts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sauternes">
      <data key="d0">Sauternes</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A French wine-producing region in the Graves section of Bordeaux, referenced in the generated sample text describing a wine individual.&lt;SEP&gt;Sauternes is a sweet white wine category described in the generation experiments as having strong flavor and produced from Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon grapes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILPNLG">
      <data key="d0">ILPNLG</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation system that jointly performs content selection and sentence aggregation to produce concise texts.&lt;SEP&gt;An Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation system whose model complexity grows exponentially with sentence limits and available facts.&lt;SEP&gt;ILPNLG is an integer linear programming-based natural language generation model evaluated for sentence aggregation and text compactness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILPNLGExtend">
      <data key="d0">ILPNLGExtend</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An extended version of the ILPNLG system developed to handle varying name lengths, conjunctions, and multiple alternative natural language names across ontologies.&lt;SEP&gt;ILPNLGExtend is an extended integer linear programming natural language generation system designed to factor in natural language name lengths and conjunctions in semantic relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline System">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard pipeline-based natural language generation system used as a baseline for text generation comparison.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipelineshort System">
      <data key="d0">Pipelineshort System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pipeline natural language generation system variant designed to produce shorter, more concise text representations than the baseline pipeline.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILP Solver">
      <data key="d0">ILP Solver</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A computational mathematical solver used in the ILPNLG framework to solve integer linear programming formulations for text generation.&lt;SEP&gt;An optimization solver utilized within ILPNLG to rapidly compute optimal fact selections and sentence aggregations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sauvignon Blanc">
      <data key="d0">Sauvignon Blanc</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A grape variety categorized in the Wine Ontology, used as an ingredient fact in generating wine descriptions.&lt;SEP&gt;Sauvignon Blanc is a varietal and category of white wine used in the natural language generation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Sauvignon Blanc is a white grape variety used in the production of Sauternes wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semillon">
      <data key="d0">Semillon</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A grape variety categorized in the Wine Ontology, featured as a component grape in wine generation facts.&lt;SEP&gt;Semillon is a grape variety used in the production of Sauternes wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Plans">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Plans</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Domain-dependent generation resources authored to verbalize ontological relations, configured to provide up to three plans per relation.&lt;SEP&gt;Domain-dependent generation resources that provide linguistic templates for verbalizing individual relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Text Plans">
      <data key="d0">Text Plans</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Domain-dependent generation resources authored for structuring content and sentences from ontologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3e6f5ef1c1e5d9ee0f856be6077fcf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chateau D'ychem">
      <data key="d0">Chateau D'ychem</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Chateau D'ychem is a wine estate and producer identified in the natural language generation sample texts as the maker of Sauternes wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Schloss Volrad">
      <data key="d0">Schloss Volrad</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Schloss Volrad is a wine producer identified in the natural language generation sample texts as the producer of Riesling wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computer Science Students">
      <data key="d0">Computer Science Students</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A group of six undergraduate and graduate computer science students who served as human evaluators, rating texts generated by natural language generation systems based on fluency, structure, and clarity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Evaluation Experiment">
      <data key="d0">Human Evaluation Experiment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation in which six students scored 104 generated texts across criteria including sentence fluency, text structure, and clarity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Electronics Experiment">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Electronics Experiment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A second series of natural language generation experiments evaluating longer texts generated using the Consumer Electronics Ontology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grapes">
      <data key="d0">Grapes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of fruit varieties, such as Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon, referenced as raw materials used in the production of wines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8156f79441beb0b0b1139fc3186002ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILPNLGAPPROX">
      <data key="d0">ILPNLGAPPROX</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An approximation model of ILPNLG that processes fact subsets separately to achieve near-linear solver times while maintaining similar facts-per-word ratios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experiments With The Consumer Electronics Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Experiments With The Consumer Electronics Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An experimental evaluation analyzing the computational efficiency and fact-per-word output of various text generation systems using the Consumer Electronics Ontology.&lt;SEP&gt;The experimental study where 60 generated texts describing consumer electronics were evaluated by human student judges for criteria such as clarity and overall quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experiments With The Wine Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Experiments With The Wine Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A previous set of evaluation experiments used as a baseline comparison for solver times and text generation metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;An experimental evaluation in which human judges scored texts generated from the Wine Ontology across several linguistic criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Development Individuals">
      <data key="d0">Development Individuals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The set of 30 individual ontology entities used as test cases for generating English texts in the experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NL Names">
      <data key="d0">NL Names</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural language names assigned per individual and class within the ontology to facilitate linguistic text generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Aggregated Sentences">
      <data key="d0">Aggregated Sentences</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Composite sentences formed by combining multiple simple fact-expressing sentences up to a maximum distinct element limit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIBREF10">
      <data key="d0">BIBREF10</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A prior research work providing baseline generation resources, sentence aggregation limits, and experimental benchmarks for consumer electronics text generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3398536fe243ccad5c6888ceecfc5e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sony">
      <data key="d0">Sony</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Sony is a multinational consumer electronics corporation whose product, the Sony DCR-TRV270 camcorder, is featured in the natural language text generation examples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experiments With The Disease Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Experiments With The Disease Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A research experiment generating texts for 200 development classes of the Disease Ontology using various natural language generation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Student Evaluators">
      <data key="d0">Student Evaluators</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A cohort of six students who participated in the subjective evaluation experiments, rating generated texts from ontologies on clarity and overall quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILP Approach">
      <data key="d0">ILP Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An Integer Linear Programming-based natural language generation methodology designed to jointly optimize fact selection and sentence planning for concise text aggregation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pipeline NLG Systems">
      <data key="d0">Pipeline NLG Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Traditional pipeline-based natural language generation architectures that perform content selection and linguistic realization sequentially.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sony DCR-TRV270">
      <data key="d0">Sony DCR-TRV270</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A digital camcorder model whose specifications are utilized as sample data to compare the text outputs of the NLG systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffe44690fdfc0faa73e0db61f9d33f01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nephropathia Epidemica">
      <data key="d0">Nephropathia Epidemica</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Nephropathia Epidemica is a disease category featured as an example class within the Disease Ontology experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Puumala Virus">
      <data key="d0">Puumala Virus</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Puumala virus is a viral pathogen identified in the text as the causative agent of nephropathia epidemica.&lt;SEP&gt;The Puumala virus is a viral pathogen mentioned in relation to voles in the introductory fragment of the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bank Voles">
      <data key="d0">Bank Voles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bank voles are a rodent species identified as the biological reservoir and origin host of the puumala virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hemorrhagic Fever With Renal Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Hemorrhagic Fever With Renal Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hemorrhagic fever with renal syndrome is a disease class of which nephropathia epidemica is specified as a clinical variant.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PipelineShort">
      <data key="d0">PipelineShort</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">PipelineShort is a variant baseline natural language generation system designed to generate shorter texts than the standard pipeline system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILPNLGApprox">
      <data key="d0">ILPNLGApprox</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">ILPNLGApprox is an approximation-oriented variant of the ILPNLG system suitable for complex ontology datasets with larger fact and sentence spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ee8473791f059fcb85f0a720e5036b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stonleigh">
      <data key="d0">Stonleigh</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Stonleigh is a wine producer mentioned as the maker of a Sauvignon Blanc wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Marciniak">
      <data key="d0">Marciniak</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher who, alongside Strube, proposed an integer linear programming (ILP) approach for combining classifier decisions in language processing problems such as route direction generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Marciniak is a researcher who co-proposed an integer linear programming approach for language processing and route direction generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voles">
      <data key="d0">Voles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voles are small rodents mentioned in the text in connection with the Puumala virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experiments with the Wine Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Experiments with the Wine Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Experiments with the Wine Ontology refers to the series of experimental evaluations conducted using wine domain data to test natural language generation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experiments with the Disease Ontology">
      <data key="d0">Experiments with the Disease Ontology</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Experiments with the Disease Ontology refers to earlier experimental evaluations using disease domain data mentioned for comparison.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ccf1d827990dd6a5adc3c9f90a8f419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Barzilay">
      <data key="d0">Barzilay</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher who, together with Lapata, investigated optimization and integer linear programming approaches for content selection and sentence aggregation in natural language generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Althaus">
      <data key="d0">Althaus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher who demonstrated that sentence ordering to maximize local coherence is equivalent to the traveling salesman problem and provided an integer linear programming formulation for it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Kuznetsova">
      <data key="d0">Kuznetsova</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher who utilized integer linear programming models for object selection, ordering, and phrase lexicalization in generating image captions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concept-To-Text Generation">
      <data key="d0">Concept-To-Text Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The automated generation of multi-sentence natural language texts directly from formal conceptual representations, databases, or ontologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Ordering">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Ordering</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The task of arranging a sequence of sentences or facts to maximize text coherence, shown to be NP-complete and related to the traveling salesman problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Traveling Salesman Problem">
      <data key="d0">Traveling Salesman Problem</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classic NP-complete combinatorial optimization problem to which local sentence coherence ordering has been shown equivalent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Image Caption Generation">
      <data key="d0">Image Caption Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multimodal generation task that uses computer vision classifiers and text generation techniques to describe the contents of images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Document Text Summarization">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Document Text Summarization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language processing task that condenses information across multiple text documents into a unified summary, often using joint optimization ILP models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sentence Compression">
      <data key="d0">Sentence Compression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A text-to-text generation task aimed at shortening a sentence while retaining its core grammatical meaning, frequently formulated via ILP.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Joint Optimization">
      <data key="d0">Joint Optimization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An optimization paradigm where multiple interdependent subtasks or decisions are modeled and solved simultaneously rather than in a sequential pipeline.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6575c1afc788be74bd028dfc616620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recurrent Neural Layers">
      <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Layers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recurrent neural layers are deep learning architectural components used to model sequential data and fuse feature information across multiple related tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Sentence Concept-To-Text Generation">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Sentence Concept-To-Text Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-sentence concept-to-text generation is a process within natural language generation focusing on converting structured ontology knowledge into fluent multi-sentence texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99df0a2940e224839126173e8c2bc846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single-Task Learning">
      <data key="d0">Single-Task Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard supervised learning approach where a dedicated model is trained independently on a single specific task with its own dataset and objective function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Cardinality Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Cardinality Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A perspective of multi-task learning where tasks share similar characteristics but differ in cardinality parameters, such as sequence lengths or number of target classes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Domain Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Domain Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multi-task learning perspective involving tasks spanning different domains or subject areas, such as product reviews across varying item types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Objective Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Objective Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A multi-task learning scenario where tasks are designed for distinct goals or objectives, such as sentiment analysis, topic categorization, and question type judgment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Matching">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Matching</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural language processing task focused on determining the degree of semantic correspondence or relevance between two text units.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recursive Neural Networks">
      <data key="d0">Recursive Neural Networks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A class of deep neural networks that process hierarchical, tree-structured inputs to compute compositional vector representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Neural Bag-Of-Words">
      <data key="d0">Neural Bag-Of-Words</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A simple neural network architecture that computes continuous representations of text by aggregating word vector embeddings without sequential modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Topic Classification">
      <data key="d0">Topic Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A text classification sub-task dedicated to organizing and categorizing documents into distinct topic-based themes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Question Type Judgment">
      <data key="d0">Question Type Judgment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification task in natural language processing aimed at categorizing user inquiries based on expected answer types or intent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d95ef3b7585c8c501112f173f330c95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Long Short-Term Memory Network">
      <data key="d0">Long Short-Term Memory Network</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A variant of recurrent neural networks equipped with internal memory cells and gating mechanisms to address gradient vanishing and exploding problems and capture long-term dependencies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Task Learning Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Task Learning Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A generalized neural network framework designed to jointly learn multiple text classification tasks in parallel using specialized intra-task and inter-task recurrent neural layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Layer">
      <data key="d0">Single Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An intra-task LSTM-based recurrent neural network layer dedicated to individual task representation learning within the multi-task framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coupling Layer">
      <data key="d0">Coupling Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An inter-task architectural layer designed to model direct pair-wise interactions and information exchange between tasks via gating mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Fusion Layer">
      <data key="d0">Local Fusion Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A shared bi-directional LSTM layer designed to facilitate indirect pair-wise interactions between tasks through concatenated inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Global Fusion Layer">
      <data key="d0">Global Fusion Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A core structural component of the neural network architecture composed of a bi-directional LSTM layer that computes global fusion terms and memory storage across tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared bi-directional LSTM layer providing global memory storage to capture shared representations across all learning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784f828261b96cc3c6df35aff5b1cae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIBREF12">
      <data key="d0">BIBREF12</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher or author cited for proposing the original Long Short-Term Memory network architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIBREF13">
      <data key="d0">BIBREF13</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A researcher or author cited for providing the specific LSTM implementation referenced and adapted in the proposed multi-task architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bi-directional LSTM">
      <data key="d0">Bi-directional LSTM</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A variant of the Long Short-Term Memory network that processes sequential information in both forward and backward directions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gradient Vanishing and Exploding">
      <data key="d0">Gradient Vanishing and Exploding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mathematical challenge during backpropagation in recurrent neural networks where gradient vectors grow or decay exponentially over long sequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gating Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Gating Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Algorithmic control structures used to regulate, filter, and balance the flow of information and memory retention within neural layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fully Connected Layer">
      <data key="d0">Fully Connected Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A standard dense neural network layer connecting the hidden states of recurrent layers to the softmax output layer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intra-Task Learning">
      <data key="d0">Intra-Task Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of learning feature representations dedicated to a single specific task within a multi-task learning framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inter-Task Interaction">
      <data key="d0">Inter-Task Interaction</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The exchange and coordination of information across different tasks, either directly pair-wise or indirectly via shared fusion mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d90ca4cd35ecf011b4a784edca91c3a</data>
    </node>
