      <data key="d0">Bidirectional Long Short Term Memory</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of recurrent neural network architectures commonly used as a shared parameter layer in sequence tagging and joint learning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Symptom">
      <data key="d0">Symptom</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A clinical entity category targeted in medical named entity recognition, frequently serving as a central word in electronic health record entity triples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STR-Encoder">
      <data key="d0">STR-Encoder</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A modified BERT language model architecture known as the shared task representation encoder that alters the attention range of the last K layers to generate task-specific representations.&lt;SEP&gt;STR-encoder (shared task representation encoder) is an architectural model component improved from BERT that uses dynamic range attention to produce task-specific representations.&lt;SEP&gt;STR-encoder is a neural encoding component in the proposed model that learns joint features of entities and relations using MASK matrices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Focused Attention Model">
      <data key="d0">Focused Attention Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A neural network model architecture proposed for jointly learning named entity recognition and relation classification using dynamic range attention.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network model architecture proposed to jointly learn named entity recognition and relation classification using an integrated BERT parameter layer.&lt;SEP&gt;A proposed model built upon BERT to dynamically adjust attention range for joint entity and relation extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Focused Attention Model is a joint learning architecture for NER and RC based on a shared parameter approach.&lt;SEP&gt;The Focused Attention Model is the proposed deep learning architecture designed for joint named entity recognition and relation extraction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-57acb1a29c2b86c001f999352f15c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1fb2eeb8c8333a70050efefb9412104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An attention mechanism category designed to construct task-specific MASK matrices to constrain attention ranges in transformer layers.&lt;SEP&gt;An attention mechanism used to transform BERT into the STR-encoder by adjusting attention ranges across entity pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism is an attention control method that utilizes custom MASK matrices to constrain or direct word attention ranges for specific downstream tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The dynamic range attention mechanism is a category of attention mechanism used to determine and constrain the attention span of words and tokens via task-specific mask matrices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1fb2eeb8c8333a70050efefb9412104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e059280feab7e800ee2d2e025bc7cbd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Task-Specific MASK Matrix">
      <data key="d0">Task-Specific MASK Matrix</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An attention masking matrix structure used to guide the attention range of transformer layers toward relevant words for specific tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </node>
