      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An annual film award ceremony whose categories from 2009 to 2016 were used to evaluate contest outcome forecasting.&lt;SEP&gt;An annual film industry awards ceremony used as a domain for evaluating outcome forecasting from social media predictions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oscars (Academy Awards) is an annual film awards event referenced in tweet prediction models and veridicality studies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oscars (Academy Awards) is an annual film awards event used to test and evaluate outcome predictions from tweet data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oscars is an annual Academy Awards event used as a case study to extract contender tweets and analyze outcome veridicality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oscars is an annual film industry awards event featured prominently in the text as a case study for veridicality prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oscars, or Academy Awards, is an annual film awards event used in the paper as a benchmark for outcome prediction.</data>
