    <node id="Veridicality">
      <data key="d0">Veridicality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Veridicality is a linguistic and semantic category indicating whether a tweet's author believes an event will happen, scored on a 5-point scale and simplified to positive, neutral, or negative.&lt;SEP&gt;Veridicality is a linguistic property and computational classification category describing the degree of certainty or truth value an author commits to regarding a claim or future outcome.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97953bb0d586e46165fea699da6cf781&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3643b20dc5e5b3d9faa14743574ec5c</data>
