    </node>
    <node id="Portugal">
      <data key="d0">Portugal</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A European country whose Portuguese tweet dataset exhibited two performance peaks and an intermediate drop due to topic shift.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e9d6cd8b1a1f2b1ece006c42d145e4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Albania">
      <data key="d0">Albania</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A European nation whose Albanian language dataset exhibited very low annotator agreement values.&lt;SEP&gt;Albania is referenced in connection with the Albanian language sentiment analysis dataset evaluated for annotator agreement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e9d6cd8b1a1f2b1ece006c42d145e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Statista">
      <data key="d0">Statista</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Statista is a market and consumer data company that produced a report documenting global photograph volume and the proportion of food pictures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YouGov">
      <data key="d0">YouGov</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">YouGov is an international research data and analytics company that conducted a poll regarding Americans taking pictures of their food.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Instagram">
      <data key="d0">Instagram</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Instagram is a prominent photo- and video-sharing social media service that facilitates user food photography sharing.&lt;SEP&gt;Instagram is a social media platform used to source user-specific food images for image processing and classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MyFitnessPal">
      <data key="d0">MyFitnessPal</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">MyFitnessPal is a nutrition and fitness tracking application that requires users to manually input meal data to log food intake.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Han Su">
      <data key="d0">Han Su</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Han Su is a researcher who studied whether recipe cuisines can be predicted from their ingredients and identified common ingredients across cuisines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ueda">
      <data key="d0">Ueda</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ueda is a researcher who proposed a personalized recipe recommendation method based on users' food preferences derived from browsing and cooking history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Yang">
      <data key="d0">Yang</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Yang is a researcher who proposed a method for food item recognition using spatial relationships between ingredients and soft pixel-level image segmentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S Jayaraman">
      <data key="d0">S Jayaraman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">S Jayaraman is a researcher who examined cultural diffusion among cuisines and tested the performance of various classifiers under unsupervised learning methods.&lt;SEP&gt;S Jayaraman is a researcher who, along with colleagues, explored the performance of various classifiers for cuisine datasets under unsupervised learning methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H Holste">
      <data key="d0">H Holste</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">H Holste is a researcher whose work focuses on predicting the cuisine of a recipe based on ingredients and assessing model performance with and without tf-idf scoring.&lt;SEP&gt;H Holste is a researcher whose work focuses on predicting the cuisine of a recipe based on its ingredient list.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cuisine Preference Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Cuisine Preference Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cuisine Preference Modeling is a research category focused on deducing individual culinary preferences and cuisines from food images and ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personalized Recommendation Systems">
      <data key="d0">Personalized Recommendation Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personalized Recommendation Systems is a technological domain aimed at tailoring suggestions to individual users based on extracted profiles and preferences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DJIA30">
      <data key="d0">DJIA30</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">DJIA30 refers to the Dow Jones Industrial Average 30 index or its associated sentiment analysis dataset used without merging in classifier training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Linear Support Vector Classifier">
      <data key="d0">Linear Support Vector Classifier</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Linear Support Vector Classifier (SVC) is a machine learning classification algorithm whose performance on recipe datasets was explored by S Jayaraman et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear Support Vector Classifier is a supervised machine learning classification algorithm evaluated on cuisine and recipe datasets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Random Forest Classifier">
      <data key="d0">Random Forest Classifier</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Random Forest Classifier is an ensemble learning method evaluated in cuisine prediction studies by both S Jayaraman et al. and R M Kumar et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Random Forest Classifier is an ensemble learning method that constructs multiple decision trees for classification tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6698485050fd363980b75ae23a237b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R M Kumar">
      <data key="d0">R M Kumar</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">R M Kumar is a researcher who utilized Tree Boosting algorithms, including Extreme Boost and Random Forest, to predict recipe cuisines from ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Teng">
      <data key="d0">Teng</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Teng is a researcher who analyzed substitutable ingredients through recipe reviews by creating substitute ingredient graphs and ingredient clusters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clarifai">
      <data key="d0">Clarifai</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Clarifai is an AI and computer vision company whose image recognition models (General Model, Food Model, and General Embedding Model) are used in the data processing pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Clarifai is an artificial intelligence company providing an image recognition API used to identify food dishes and ingredients from images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Yummly">
      <data key="d0">Yummly</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Yummly is a digital recipe and food platform whose recipe dataset was utilized to train the cuisine classification model.&lt;SEP&gt;Yummly is a recipe and food platform whose dataset of 39,774 recipes across 20 cuisines is analyzed to determine cuisines from ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Italian Cuisine">
      <data key="d0">Italian Cuisine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Italian cuisine is a culinary category heavily represented in the dataset and identified as a primary preference of the user.&lt;SEP&gt;Italian cuisine is a culinary category that overshadows the Yummly dataset with 7,383 associated recipes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mexican Cuisine">
      <data key="d0">Mexican Cuisine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mexican cuisine is a culinary category into which specific native dishes, such as tacos identified by image models, are classified.&lt;SEP&gt;Mexican cuisine is a food classification category identified by native dishes such as tacos and found to be one of the user's primary preferences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extreme Boost">
      <data key="d0">Extreme Boost</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Extreme Boost is a tree boosting machine learning algorithm utilized by R M Kumar et al. that demonstrated superior performance over Random Forest in predicting cuisines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clarifai General Model">
      <data key="d0">Clarifai General Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Clarifai General Model is an image recognition model recognizing over 11,000 concepts, used to distinguish food images from non-food images and detect people.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clarifai Food Model">
      <data key="d0">Clarifai Food Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Clarifai Food Model is a specialized vision recognition model identifying more than 1,000 food items down to the ingredient level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clarifai General Embedding Model">
      <data key="d0">Clarifai General Embedding Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Clarifai General Embedding Model maps input images into a 1024-dimensional vector space to detect and remove visually duplicate food images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Porter Stemmer Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">Porter Stemmer Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Porter Stemmer Algorithm is an algorithmic process used for removing morphological and inflectional suffixes from ingredient words during natural language preprocessing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc715f7f0042435219a9937b5527ecef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Kaggle">
      <data key="d0">Kaggle</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Kaggle is an online data science platform that hosts datasets and competitions, including the Yummly dataset used in the study.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Filipino Cuisine">
      <data key="d0">Filipino Cuisine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Filipino cuisine is a culinary category analyzed by the model, showing decreased classification rates at higher K values due to dataset imbalance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vietnamese Cuisine">
      <data key="d0">Vietnamese Cuisine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vietnamese cuisine is a culinary category evaluated within the cuisine classification model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cajun_Creole Cuisine">
      <data key="d0">Cajun_Creole Cuisine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cajun_Creole cuisine is a regional culinary category analyzed within the ingredient-based classification system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tacos">
      <data key="d0">Tacos</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tacos are a native Mexican dish used as an example of a meal that Clarifai can identify directly without requiring ingredient-level classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KNN Model">
      <data key="d0">KNN Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The K Nearest Neighbors Model is a machine learning classification algorithm trained on recipe ingredients to predict cuisine preferences across various k-values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rudimentary Method">
      <data key="d0">Rudimentary Method</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The rudimentary method is a baseline classification approach that maps high-probability ingredients directly to unique cuisine ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Radar Chart">
      <data key="d0">Radar Chart</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A radar chart is a data visualization format used to plot and depict the user's cuisine preferences and model predictions across different k-values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Pipeline">
      <data key="d0">Data Pipeline</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The data pipeline is an automated workflow that processes user food images, applies natural language and image processing, and feeds data into classification models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recommendation System">
      <data key="d0">Recommendation System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A proposed future suggestive system that combines determined user cuisine preferences with contextual factors such as weather and physical activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad807b208d1972a5fdf0d252a78fff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Language Processing">
      <data key="d0">Natural Language Processing</data>
