    <edge source="Byte Pair Encoding" target="Neural Machine Translation">
      <data key="d4">32.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Byte Pair Encoding was adapted from Neural Machine Translation practices, though requiring far fewer merge operations for low-resource related language pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Byte Pair Encoding was adapted in neural machine translation to limit core vocabulary size and handle open vocabulary translation.&lt;SEP&gt;Byte Pair Encoding was adapted specifically to alleviate vocabulary issues in Neural Machine Translation.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper identifies Byte Pair Encoding for neural machine translation between related languages as a key future direction.</data>
      <data key="d6">algorithmic adaptation, hyperparameter tuning&lt;SEP&gt;future research, technique adoption&lt;SEP&gt;technological application, standard algorithm&lt;SEP&gt;vocabulary reduction, subword segmentation</data>
