    <edge source="France" target="Twitter">
      <data key="d4">84.0</data>
      <data key="d5">France demonstrates over-predicted languages within the Twitter corpus.&lt;SEP&gt;Geolocated Twitter users in France were analyzed to evaluate the geographic distribution of linguistic variables and income.&lt;SEP&gt;Geolocated Twitter users were assigned to departments within France to examine spatial linguistic patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Twitter dataset was filtered to examine French-speaking users with representative home GPS locations across France.&lt;SEP&gt;The study analyzed geolocated Twitter users and their posts across France.&lt;SEP&gt;The study analyzes a massive dataset of French tweets collected from users located across France.&lt;SEP&gt;The study combined a corpus of French Twitter communications with socioeconomic census maps from France.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter data from geolocated users across France was collected to analyze spatial language use and income distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter user data and inferred GPS coordinates are analyzed and validated against official population distributions across French administrative levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter user spatial locations were mapped and validated against official population benchmarks across administrative regions in France.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter users geolocated across the departments of France provided the observational dataset for the geographic and linguistic analysis.</data>
