    <edge source="Socioeconomic Status" target="Twitter">
      <data key="d4">39.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Researchers enrich Twitter datasets with location and census information to study and infer user socioeconomic status.&lt;SEP&gt;The study demonstrates that individual socioeconomic status can be inferred from online activity, network position, and language on Twitter.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter data is combined with spatial socioeconomic indicators to study individual socioeconomic features and user behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter user activity and language were cross-referenced with socioeconomic status indicators to uncover sociolinguistic trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter user locations and activities were paired with geographic socioeconomic indicators to investigate individual socioeconomic characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d6">attribute inference, social media analysis&lt;SEP&gt;data enrichment, behavioral analysis&lt;SEP&gt;data integration, socioeconomic analysis&lt;SEP&gt;data linking, socioeconomic profiling&lt;SEP&gt;demographic inference, platform data</data>
