    </edge>
    <edge source="Binary ILP Problems" target="Extended ILP Model">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Extended ILP Model is formulated as a binary ILP problem whose variables grow exponentially with the number of fact subsets.</data>
      <data key="d6">mathematical formulation, complexity scaling</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Binary ILP Problems" target="LP Relaxation">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">LP relaxation is used as a technique to approximate solutions to binary ILP problems by dropping integer constraints.</data>
      <data key="d6">approximation method, problem relaxation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-623c9cfea2f0f1560eb4ea4b48d419c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NP-Hard" target="0-1 Multiple Knapsack Problem">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The 0-1 multiple knapsack problem is recognized as an NP-hard combinatorial problem.</data>
