    </edge>
    <edge source="Entity and Relation Extraction" target="Joint Learning">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Joint learning is an approach applied to entity and relation extraction to simultaneously learn entities and relations while capturing shared features.</data>
      <data key="d6">machine learning framework, task integration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Joint Learning" target="Bidirectional Long Short Term Memory">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bidirectional Long Short Term Memory is traditionally employed as a shared parameter layer in joint learning frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d6">baseline architecture, parameter sharing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Joint Learning" target="Focused Attention Model">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The focused attention model is designed to jointly learn named entity recognition and relation classification.&lt;SEP&gt;The focused attention model leverages joint learning to enhance performance across both NER and RC tasks.</data>
      <data key="d6">learning paradigm, model implementation&lt;SEP&gt;model objective, joint training</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f1fb2eeb8c8333a70050efefb9412104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="Focused Attention Model">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Focused Attention Model relies on the STR-encoder as its core shared parameter layer to produce representations for downstream tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR-encoder is a core component within the focused attention model that outputs hidden representations for joint learning.&lt;SEP&gt;The focused attention model incorporates the STR-encoder structure to obtain task-specific context representations.</data>
      <data key="d6">model architecture, representation encoder&lt;SEP&gt;model architecture, structural component</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="Task-Specific MASK Matrix">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">STR-encoder utilizes task-specific MASK matrices to restrict its attention range to relevant task words.</data>
      <data key="d6">mechanism implementation, attention modulation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cfda2df27b2b2e8e0d65e1812ca700fd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The STR-encoder utilizes the dynamic range attention mechanism via task-specific MASK matrices to generate targeted representations.</data>
      <data key="d6">mechanism integration, attention control</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="CLS Token">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The STR-encoder adds a CLS token at the start of input sequences following the BERT specification.</data>
      <data key="d6">tokenization standard, sequence structure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="SEP Token">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The STR-encoder attaches a SEP token at the end of input sequences as an end delimiter.</data>
      <data key="d6">sequence formatting, boundary marker</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="NER">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Parameters of the STR-encoder are shared with the downstream task layer for NER.</data>
      <data key="d6">task integration, parameter sharing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STR-Encoder" target="RC">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The STR-encoder generates outputs fed into perceptrons to predict probabilities for the RC task.</data>
      <data key="d6">task integration, representation output</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Focused Attention Model" target="NER">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Focused Attention Model is designed as a joint learning model that incorporates NER as one of its primary downstream tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The focused attention model is applied to and evaluated on the NER task, achieving a 96.89% F1-score.</data>
      <data key="d6">joint learning, downstream task&lt;SEP&gt;task application, performance evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Focused Attention Model" target="RC">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Focused Attention Model integrates RC as a downstream task within its shared parameter joint learning architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;The focused attention model performs the RC task and beats baseline models with a 96.44% F1-score.</data>
      <data key="d6">joint learning, downstream task&lt;SEP&gt;task application, performance evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Focused Attention Model" target="Joint Entity And Relation Extraction">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The focused attention model is designed for and evaluated on the joint entity and relation extraction task.</data>
      <data key="d6">task objective, joint learning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Focused Attention Model" target="Adam Optimization Algorithm">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The focused attention model is optimized using the Adam optimization algorithm with a learning rate of 10^-5.</data>
      <data key="d6">model optimization, training configuration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b74404709f6b49b2bef33ca7f921e55</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Focused Attention Model" target="Joint-Bi-LSTM">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The focused attention model is compared against the Joint-Bi-LSTM baseline across NER, RC, and joint extraction tasks.</data>
