    </edge>
    <edge source="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism" target="NER">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Dynamic range attention provides task-specific MASK matrices to focus word representations according to the requirements of the NER task.&lt;SEP&gt;The dynamic range attention mechanism determines the full unconstrained attention matrix applied during the NER downstream task.</data>
      <data key="d6">attention mechanism, task configuration&lt;SEP&gt;task adaptation, representation learning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e059280feab7e800ee2d2e025bc7cbd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism" target="RC">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Dynamic range attention provides task-specific MASK matrices to focus word representations according to the characteristics of the RC task.&lt;SEP&gt;The dynamic range attention mechanism is used to define specialized mask matrices that confine token attention ranges for the RC downstream task.</data>
      <data key="d6">attention masking, task configuration&lt;SEP&gt;task adaptation, representation learning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e059280feab7e800ee2d2e025bc7cbd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism" target="MASK Matrix">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Dynamic range attention operates by custom-designing the binary MASK matrix values to selectively allow or block attention between words.</data>
      <data key="d6">operational mechanism, attention masking</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8273db0372f06b5474e49c6b558bba7b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dynamic Range Attention Mechanism" target="STR-encoder">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The dynamic range attention mechanism transforms BERT into the STR-encoder to enrich feature representations.</data>
