    <edge source="Bilingual Lexicon Induction" target="Morphological Generalization">
      <data key="d4">36.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A central question of the research is whether bilingual lexicon induction models possess human-like morphological generalization capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Morphological generalization is evaluated to assess how well bilingual lexicon induction models handle infrequent morphological word forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Morphological generalization is introduced as an analytical framework to measure the robustness of bilingual lexicon induction models.&lt;SEP&gt;State-of-the-art bilingual lexicon induction systems are assessed on their capacity for morphological generalization across rare word inflections.</data>
      <data key="d6">evaluation, model generalization&lt;SEP&gt;linguistic capability, model evaluation&lt;SEP&gt;model capability, evaluation focus&lt;SEP&gt;model evaluation, generalization study</data>
