    <edge source="GLAD" target="GCE">
      <data key="d4">38.0</data>
      <data key="d5">GCE simplifies GLAD's architecture by removing slot-specific recurrent and self-attention layers in the encoder.&lt;SEP&gt;GCE was developed within the architectural framework of GLAD to mitigate GLAD's high latency by employing a single globally conditioned encoder.&lt;SEP&gt;GLAD and GCE are baseline models compared against each other, with GCE reducing encoder requirements relative to GLAD.&lt;SEP&gt;GLAD and GCE are existing baseline models compared against each other, with GCE reducing encoder requirements relative to GLAD.&lt;SEP&gt;GLAD and GCE are recurrent neural network-based baseline models evaluated and compared under identical training settings.</data>
