      <data key="d5">The G-SAT model contains specialized classifier final layers to model binary predictions for requestable slots.</data>
      <data key="d6">slot classification, binary prediction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-2e1e71821eb167dabc5002a21237f815</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Requestable Slots" target="StateNet_PSI">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">StateNet_PSI is incapable of predicting requestable slots, unlike the other evaluated DST models.</data>
      <data key="d6">functional constraint, slot incompatibility</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-af6147035553ac26ef0837a5ab654f4f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="StateNet" target="Pre-Trained Embeddings">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">StateNet depends on the existence of pre-trained embeddings to construct representations of user utterances and candidate slots.</data>
      <data key="d6">model dependency, semantic representation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-45dd962c5b788395b9105c9472288d6f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neural Belief Tracker" target="Pre-Trained Embeddings">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Neural Belief Tracker relies on pre-trained semantic embeddings to operate without requiring explicit semantic lexicons.</data>
      <data key="d6">feature representation, initialization</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-45dd962c5b788395b9105c9472288d6f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bidirectional-LSTM" target="G-SAT Model">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The G-SAT encoder utilizes a bidirectional-LSTM to process the concatenated user utterance and system action into hidden representations.</data>
      <data key="d6">neural architecture, component</data>
