    <edge source="Twitter" target="Facebook">
      <data key="d4">56.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Facebook and Twitter are cited together as popular social media platforms that shape current information consumption and filter bubbles.&lt;SEP&gt;The research project evaluates models and methods for linking and identifying matching user profiles across Twitter and Facebook.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter and Facebook are contrasted in how the same individual uses each platform for different thematic purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter and Facebook are social platforms whose accounts were jointly analyzed in an 11,224-account corpus to test user account matching techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter and Facebook are the two primary social networks between which user accounts are matched using temporal and linguistic patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Twitter and Facebook are the two social media platforms across which user accounts were matched in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;User accounts across both Twitter and Facebook were collected and matched to evaluate the efficacy of digital stylometry models without relying on profile information.</data>
